{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e","id":409432,"title":"Solar Redemption in 3e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-17T17:42:10-08:00","id":409432,"title":"Solar Redemption in 3e","content":"Now, as we all know, Solar &quot;Exaltations&quot; are demonic spirits that have possessed the bodies of the innocent, slowly consuming the essence of the previous host, and as they do, escalating from seemingly heroic acts (which secretly serve their dark purpose) into outright tyranny and despotism.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is a lame story-arc, and there should be alternatives.<br /> <br /> I think it would be really cool if a character who was struggling to hold onto their humanity could redeem themselves into being a Dragonblooded. Obviously this could only work if they were of the Blood of the Dragons to begin with - otherwise the best they can hope for is a swift and merciful death.<br /> <br /> Anyway, just wondering if there'll be any mechanics to support this!<br /> <br /> <br /> /end sarcasm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T17:49:48-08:00","id":409459,"title":"","content":"I'm not really sure what this post is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T17:53:19-08:00","id":409463,"title":"","content":"This would only work if the majority of Solars actually descended into despotism. Otherwise it would undermine the whole purpose of having Solars in the game. I suggest a mechanic to be added during character creation to see if your character is part of the 1% that would fight against the demonic spirit inhabiting their soul. The the other 99% of characters must play an evil Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T18:27:52-08:00","id":409475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409459#post409459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sure what this post is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I belive this entire thread is a mockery of the Abyssal/Infernal Redemption thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T18:28:56-08:00","id":409477,"title":"","content":"There's only one way to redeem a Solar: jade weapons through the skull. I call it the &quot;Pelleps Delled method&quot;.<br /> <br /> Allowing Solars a method for redemption would detract from the existential horror of playing a body-hopping millenia-old demon. Pretty soon, most Solars would be angsting around, writing poetry and trying to redeem themselves, possibly wielding 2 scimitars.<br /> <br /> If you want to play a Dragonblood, play a Dragonblood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T18:37:54-08:00","id":409483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409459#post409459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sure what this post is about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How irritating and stupid I find the incessant Redemption threads, mostly. In-setting, Solars aren't the thing people aspire to be, they're the bogeymen and monsters of myth.<br /> <br /> <br /> There is no objective standard of right, wrong, or evil in the setting. The Unconquered Sun is a glorified crack addict, the beings who created the world literally made mankind to suffer (and got stuffed into a box made of their own guts as repayment), the First Age Solars were monsters of such epic proportions that their loyal lieutenants and advisors dug up heroic willpower to resist their beyond-god-like power to influence the minds of others to brutally murder them all, and the current guys in charge of Creation haven't done so well either.<br /> <br /> On a metaphysical level, everyone is covered in shit and bad choices, and the good guys are those who are doing good things right now.<br /> <br /> If you want to redeem yourself for your bad choices in life, go forth and do good deeds. Wanting a little gold star for the effort is bloody *kindergarten* morality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T18:57:04-08:00","id":409490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409483#post409483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to redeem yourself for your bad choices in life, go forth and do good deeds. Wanting a little gold star for the effort is bloody *kindergarten* morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>You.<br /> <br /> I like you. &lt;3<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T19:12:19-08:00","id":409494,"title":"","content":"If there's no objective standard of evil/right/wrong, how can you say there are people doing good things? What does good even look like in such a setting?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wanting a little gold star for the effort is bloody *kindergarten* morality. </div> </div> </div>Are there redemption stories where the character *isn't* rewarded in some way for changing? Would you be interested in telling a story where nobody cared about the changes a character had made to both themselves as well as the good deeds they've done for others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T19:14:26-08:00","id":409496,"title":"","content":"Redemption stories often end with the character being rewarded with dying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T19:44:12-08:00","id":409505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409494#post409494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's no objective standard of evil/right/wrong, how can you say there are people doing good things? What does good even look like in such a setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the root of all philosophical debate ever since the existence of God stopped being axiomatic. In such a world, good and evil are ultimately defined by the individual and each definition is meaningless to others, as they will likely as not lack your exact same frame of values. Which system prevails is ultimately decided by which one kills all the other ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T19:47:52-08:00","id":409507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409505#post409505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Welcome to the root of all philosophical debate ever since the existence of God stopped being axiomatic. In such a world, good and evil are ultimately defined by the individual and each definition is meaningless to others, as they will likely as not lack your exact same frame of values. Which system prevails is ultimately decided by which one kills all the other ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes - that was my point. SuperG talked about how &quot;the good guys are those who are doing good things right now&quot; just after saying there was no objective right/wrong/evil. How can anyone do good if there's no objective right/wrong (or rather, what do you measure their good deeds by and why that over something else)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T19:50:27-08:00","id":409508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409507#post409507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yes - that was my point. SuperG talked about how &quot;the good guys are those who are doing good things right now&quot; just after saying there was no objective right/wrong/evil. How can anyone do good if there's no objective right/wrong (or rather, what do you measure their good deeds by and why that over something else)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pick a system of belief. Punch everyone who does something that disagrees with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T20:28:20-08:00","id":409545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409494#post409494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's no objective standard of evil/right/wrong, how can you say there are people doing good things?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't, objectively. You can, however, say it subjectively, which is kind of the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does good even look like in such a setting? </div> </div> </div>Exactly the same as it looks in our world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T20:44:31-08:00","id":409572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409545#post409545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly the same as it looks in our world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that people like me insist otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T21:08:13-08:00","id":409623,"title":"","content":"In the real world, people argue about what is good and bad, right and wrong.<br /> That doesn't mean there is no objective right and wrong. We just don't know what it is.<br /> <br /> Same for Exalted. Just because the Unconquered Sun is a dick, doesn't mean things aren't still objectively right and wrong. It's just the writers aren't going to say &quot;X is right, Y is wrong&quot;, that's for you to talk about in games.<br /> <br /> The fact that people don't know what objective morality is, doesn't mean it doesn't exist. In both the real world and the setting.<br /> <br /> But that's slightly different to Abyssal redemption. I do see the argument here.<br /> There is no objectively good force that makes sure all good people are suitably rewarded. No karma, no heaven. So, how does the Abyssal know what is good? Who determines when he can become a Solar? It doesn't make a lot of sense. It's not like his exaltation knows what's good. Possibly if he's good by the Unconquered Sun's standards?<br /> Personally, I'd prefer Abyssals to turn into Solars through researching powerful magic, rather than being &quot;good&quot;. I could say promoting life as being appropriate for turning them into a Solar. That might mean they end up doing things some might consider bad (like, I don't know, stopping women having abortions maybe?) or whatever, but it's obviously against the Neverborn.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd rather play an Abyssal who just tries to be good, than one who turns into a Solar. If I wanted to play a Solar, I'd play a Solar.<br /> I would consider it cool to dramatically sacrifice myself to stop the Neverborn, and this cleanse my exaltation so the next guy can be a Solar.<br /> But obviously others want to do this, and I don't want to stop their fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-18-2015, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T00:45:39-08:00","id":409776,"title":"","content":"The thing about Abyssal 'redemption' is that is it not actually about good and evil. It's about changing from being Oblivion oriented to Creation oriented. It is possible to make a philosophical argument that the death and final obliteration of all things is not only inevitable, but desirable right now - it's just a grim argument and most people aren't going to be convinced because human beings aren't very good at viewing their own existences through a rationalist lens (and there are evolutionary imperative not to).<br /> <br /> <i>Being</i> an Abyssal, irrespective of any actions a character takes, means being aligned towards oblivion. Your very essence rebels against the essence of Creation - you are quite literally not a part of the living world anymore. Even if - to borrow the Reclamation plotline for a second - a circle of heroic Abyssals were to throw down the Ebon Dragon and save Creation from demon rule, they would be unable to claim that victory. Creation can never, ever welcome them. They cannot have a home among the living, or even truly among the dead.<br /> <br /> 'Redemption' for Abyssals is about turning away from Oblivion and embracing living existence - returning to the state of a forceful expression of Creation, a Lawgiver whose very existence solidifies, supports, and expands the world out of formless chaos. Redemption doesn't mean becoming good again, it means returning to champion life over the end of all.<br /> <br /> Most of the examples we pick as actions along that path follow a traditional moral conception of 'good' while most pro-Oblivion actions follow a moral conception of 'evil' but this has to do with he origin of human moral schema - no one wants to be killed so killing is outlawed. Theoretically an abyssal could return to status as a champion of Creation through actions most observers would consider utterly horrible - serving as a champion of Ma-Ha-Suchi's cause for instance.<br /> <br /> In the inverse, an Abyssal can absolutely do 'good' in the eyes of most people and still be promoting Oblivion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T01:31:52-08:00","id":409789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409776#post409776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about Abyssal 'redemption' is that is it not actually about good and evil. It's about changing from being Oblivion oriented to Creation oriented. It is possible to make a philosophical argument that the death and final obliteration of all things is not only inevitable, but desirable right now - it's just a grim argument and most people aren't going to be convinced because human beings aren't very good at viewing their own existences through a rationalist lens (and there are evolutionary imperative not to).<br /> <br /> <i>Being</i> an Abyssal, irrespective of any actions a character takes, means being aligned towards oblivion. Your very essence rebels against the essence of Creation - you are quite literally not a part of the living world anymore. Even if - to borrow the Reclamation plotline for a second - a circle of heroic Abyssals were to throw down the Ebon Dragon and save Creation from demon rule, they would be unable to claim that victory. Creation can never, ever welcome them. They cannot have a home among the living, or even truly among the dead.<br /> <br /> 'Redemption' for Abyssals is about turning away from Oblivion and embracing living existence - returning to the state of a forceful expression of Creation, a Lawgiver whose very existence solidifies, supports, and expands the world out of formless chaos. Redemption doesn't mean becoming good again, it means returning to champion life over the end of all.<br /> <br /> Most of the examples we pick as actions along that path follow a traditional moral conception of 'good' while most pro-Oblivion actions follow a moral conception of 'evil' but this has to do with he origin of human moral schema - no one wants to be killed so killing is outlawed. Theoretically an abyssal could return to status as a champion of Creation through actions most observers would consider utterly horrible - serving as a champion of Ma-Ha-Suchi's cause for instance.<br /> <br /> In the inverse, an Abyssal can absolutely do 'good' in the eyes of most people and still be promoting Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Abyssal &quot;Redemption&quot;, as written here, is toxic both to Infernals, Solars and indeed the entire game line. It's toxic to Infernals, because by putting the cliched, hackneyed story of REDEMPTION! in, you make Solars into LAWFUL GOOD! (as written by bad authors), and we get the endless &quot;how to cure the tainted corruption of these!?!&quot;. It's toxic to Solars, because it easily and swiftly shorthands Solars as axiomatic good guys - after all, their anima is flaring the &quot;right&quot; colour, they MUST be the good guys. It's toxic to the game line as a whole because suddenly there's this concept that you can get takebacks - you can UNchange things, put the genie back in the bottle, and get rid of Abyssals and all their nasty queries and plot threads.<br /> <br /> <br /> So no. Abyssal/Solar conversions shouldn't be a thing. At least not in such a way that it's a straightforward and obvious fix to a problem. <br /> <br /> <br /> Hey, here's an idea: Abyssals that don't flip back to Solars. They transform into a third thing: the Chosen of Lethe. Glowing gold if you insist, but still inherently tied to the dead - but as protector and shepherd, not killer.<br /> <br /> Or heck, this is a good place to stick &quot;the Chosen of ME!&quot; - they get to rebuild themselves into a form they (in that moment) approve of, breaking the rules laid down by Sun and Oblivion alike.<br /> <br /> <br /> And moving the world *onwards* to something *different*, rather than rolling back the clock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T02:52:30-08:00","id":409844,"title":"","content":"So to sum up this thread in a single sentence.<br /> <br /> Solar Redemption is a Mary Sue optimization choice that creates a toxic disbalance for Dragon Blooded protagonism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T03:38:51-08:00","id":409859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409776#post409776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about Abyssal 'redemption' is that is it not actually about good and evil. It's about changing from being Oblivion oriented to Creation oriented. It is possible to make a philosophical argument that the death and final obliteration of all things is not only inevitable, but desirable right now - it's just a grim argument and most people aren't going to be convinced because human beings aren't very good at viewing their own existences through a rationalist lens (and there are evolutionary imperative not to).<br /> <br /> <i>Being</i> an Abyssal, irrespective of any actions a character takes, means being aligned towards oblivion. Your very essence rebels against the essence of Creation - you are quite literally not a part of the living world anymore. Even if - to borrow the Reclamation plotline for a second - a circle of heroic Abyssals were to throw down the Ebon Dragon and save Creation from demon rule, they would be unable to claim that victory. Creation can never, ever welcome them. They cannot have a home among the living, or even truly among the dead.<br /> <br /> 'Redemption' for Abyssals is about turning away from Oblivion and embracing living existence - returning to the state of a forceful expression of Creation, a Lawgiver whose very existence solidifies, supports, and expands the world out of formless chaos. Redemption doesn't mean becoming good again, it means returning to champion life over the end of all.<br /> <br /> Most of the examples we pick as actions along that path follow a traditional moral conception of 'good' while most pro-Oblivion actions follow a moral conception of 'evil' but this has to do with he origin of human moral schema - no one wants to be killed so killing is outlawed. Theoretically an abyssal could return to status as a champion of Creation through actions most observers would consider utterly horrible - serving as a champion of Ma-Ha-Suchi's cause for instance.<br /> <br /> In the inverse, an Abyssal can absolutely do 'good' in the eyes of most people and still be promoting Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is precisely why tying Abyssals so close to Oblivion is a bad thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T06:17:51-08:00","id":410007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409789#post409789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or heck, this is a good place to stick &quot;the Chosen of ME!&quot; - they get to rebuild themselves into a form they (in that moment) approve of, breaking the rules laid down by Sun and Oblivion alike.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>3E Devil Tigers confirmed to Be Abyssals instead of Infernals!<br /> <br /> Everybody Lose Shit!</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T07:53:49-08:00","id":410089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409844#post409844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So to sum up this thread in a single sentence.<br /> <br /> Solar Redemption is a Mary Sue optimization choice that creates a toxic disbalance for Dragon Blooded protagonism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like you too. So much. Right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>3E Devil Tigers confirmed to Be Abyssals instead of Infernals!<br /> <br /> Everybody Lose Shit!</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Abyssals confirmed to wield Neverborn charms!<br /> <br /> The fallen titans shall rise again!</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:17:54-08:00","id":410163,"title":"","content":"Redemption doesn't make sense in 2e because every Solar was written as a banally evil fuckwit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:41:40-08:00","id":410211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410163#post410163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Redemption doesn't make sense in 2e because every Solar was written as a banally evil fuckwit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hardly, if it was so you wouldn't be seeing so much people objecting to Redemption for thematic reasons like right now in this very thread. You'll have a lot more people protesting that Solars are dicks through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:48:23-08:00","id":410234,"title":"","content":"I actually kinda like the idea of Infernal redemption. Assuming that, according to the Infernal preview that got sent out a while back, Infernals are still meant to represent the glories, horrors, beauty and debauchery of the First Age, and are still meant to be the Yozi's special snowflake and that they live vicariously though, their redemption arch would involve them moving past all that and realizing that the world is more than just a tool to provide them enjoyment.<br /> <br /> Granted, that's a shitton of assumptions, but I like the idea of it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:51:51-08:00","id":410245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410211#post410211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hardly, if it was so you wouldn't be seeing so much people objecting to Redemption for <b>thematic</b> reasons like right now in this very thread. You'll have a lot more people protesting that Solars are dicks through.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think that word means what you think it does. I see pattern recognition, but not proof of theme. What is being discussed here is a motif, not a theme.<br /> <br /> And the &quot;theme&quot; of the Solars is almost meaningless to individual Solars. Similarly, characters in Creation have ideas about what constitutes good and evil, regardless of what the truth is, because they aren't being written from a meta standpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":86,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","user":"John M\u00f8rke","date":".  typo 02-18-2015, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:52:42-08:00","id":410246,"title":"","content":"I'm cool with Abyssal Redemption because it suits their themes, but I'd rather it be a remote, rumoured thing without mechanics behind it, like Golconda in vampire. Infernal Redemption seems less in the wheelhouse of infernals, who don't really have the &quot;dark curse&quot; motif going on, but I don't know much about 3e infernals, so I can take it or leave it. Redemption definitely shouldn't be the sort of thing a player can comfortably assume they'll be able to achieve in the course of a game, though, and IMO there probably don't need to be rules for it, because that makes it feel a bit too immediate, and the rules never really gave you that much you couldn't get from common sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:56:25-08:00","id":410255,"title":"","content":"Abyssal Redemption &amp; Vampire the Masquerade:<br /> <br /> Vampire had <b>a lot</b> of &quot;end of the world&quot; worries.<ul><li>First, each generation was weaker than the previous (think of it like Dragon-Blooded Breeding.... each generation, the purity diminishes).</li> <li>Second, there was a prophesy about &quot;the end times&quot; being marked by &quot;Thin-Blooded&quot;.<ul><li>Imagine if Abyssal Exalts heard a whisper that the world will end when Abyssal Half-Castes arrive. Then, in modern times, there are a bunch of Half-Castes.</li> <li>Of if we can use the Dragon-Blooded Breeding example, if they had Half-Castes, the Dragon-Blooded begin <i>freaking the fuck out</i> to see children born <i>weird</i>. Terrestrials with no anima banners. Or Terrestrials without a clear Aspect. Or Terrestrials who can't master anything above Essence 2 or 3.</li> </ul></li> <li>Lastly, each Vampire bloodline had a founder - who was still intimately connected to their clan. They <i>defined</i> their clans, as the first of their lineages, and the Eldest of these lineages was tied to all their progeny.<ul><li>Again, in Exalted terms, imagine each Deathlord being the founder of their &quot;Abyssal&quot; clans -- anything you can do, they can do better. They are <i>gods</i> compared to you.</li> <li>Or for Dragon-Blooded, imagine each House founder was immortal <b>and </b>had those Dynasty keyword charms -- so they could wreak horrors upon and through their progeny.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <b>So imagine Vampires as a hybrid between Abyssals &amp; Dragon-Blooded. All of the Abyssal powers and curses --- but they reproduce via blood, passing on a Breeding score like Dragon-Blooded.</b><br /> <br /> When the end of the world finally came?<ul><li>In Exalted terms, imagine all the &quot;Vampires&quot; begin seeing their <i>maximum Essence cap</i> reduced. All Essence 10 were reduced to Essence 9. A few weeks later, 9 were reduced to 8. A few weeks more, 8 was reduced to 7. Then 7 to 6. <b>This had many wonderful ramifications</b>.<ul><li>First, the Essence 10 Vampires are reduced to Essence 9. The eldest &amp; most powerful -- are also paranoid and isolated. They had no way of seeing this was a species-wide thing (since so few exist at the highest Essence cap), so they thought the curse was a <b>personal</b> thing. Being paranoid &amp; disempowered, it eliminated the very &quot;apocalypse&quot; everyone feared because none of them would dare go apeshit with their powers, too afraid they were the only weak one (and that their enemies were waiting for them to show their faces, to finally one-up them).</li> </ul></li> <li>Second, some discover that cannibalism restores their powers. Essentially, you either grew weaker -- or killed each other. Which is it? Are you prey or predator?<ul><li>Imagine if Abyssals found their Necromantic spells waning and had to cannibalize other Abyssals to restore their mastery over the dead.</li> <li>Or if Dragon-Blooded could temporarily improve their Breeding again by eating other Terrestrials.</li> </ul></li> <li>Third, that part about the Thin-Blood? They may be weak - but they're still Vampires - so some Elders begin feeding on them. Others, seeing them as an omen of the end-times, simply murder them en masse whenever they find them.<ul><li>.....and that part I mentioned about every Elder having &quot;Dynast&quot; style charms? Now those paranoid Elders, who are losing power, <b>also</b> detect that their progeny are being mass-murdered. <i><b>More</b></i> paranoia. So they begin braving the world and feeding on their rivals (and <i>their</i> progeny) to even the score.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> All the while, this is all kept fairly discrete - for the same reason, in Exalted terms, that a bunch of Abyssals or Dragon-Blooded wouldn't want to go public (and let Sidereals &amp; Solars discover their weakness).<br /> <br /> *<br /> *<br /> <br /> <b>By the time this new &quot;curse&quot; </b>reaches Essence 6 -- and Essence 6 becomes Essence 5 - now we're talking things accelerating <i><b>to days</b></i>, each transition coming faster and faster. This is where most characters fall.<br /> <br /> The Scenario for characters was written with them taking shelter in a <b><i>church</i></b>. Even if you're non-religious, the idea was that those prowling the night were preying on each other or falling weaker - but the church served as a sanctuary of sorts, so you all decide to hide indoors. <br /> <br /> So a bunch of Abyssals begin hiding in Solar Manses -- simply because it's a good hiding place. Inside, there are other Abyssals too -- all trying to avoid the chaos of what's happening outside.<br /> <br /> *<br /> *<br /> *<br /> <br /> <b>Surviving</b> (and &quot;Winning&quot;) the scenario...... required doing nothing at all.<br /> <br /> *<br /> *<br /> *<br /> <br /> What the end-game scenario reminded us was that <b>Vampirism was the curse -- </b>and <i>it had been weakening</i>. Each generation was &quot;weaker&quot; than the previous because it was &quot;less damned&quot;. The Thin-Blood are proof that it had reached a point that many of the strongest &quot;curses&quot; were relenting --- hence, some who could eat, others who could resist the sun, some get pregnant, etc. <i><b>They were human</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Did you spend the end-times cannibalizing your peers for power? You're <b>a monster</b>. <br /> Did you kill your rivals when they grew weak, for whatever reason? You're <b>a monster</b>.<br /> Did you (anything normally considered horrific), etc.....<br /> When the &quot;curse&quot; ends, you hit Essence 1 and your body aged to it's true-age, leaving piles of dust and bones in many cases.<br /> <br /> <b>Characters who do no such thing</b>...... hit Essence 1.....and are human once more. No curse. No damnation. People die every day - but you're given a new chance. You had power and some horrific curse - but if you cleaved to what made you human, despite it all, you return that way again.<br /> <br /> *<br /> *<br /> *<br /> *<br /> <br /> So yeah, Abyssals needing to run around like goth bish boys have a strong &quot;aura&quot; of Mary Sue when &quot;Redemption&quot; means turning into golden god-kings as opposed to.... I dunno..... simply wanting a second chance at life (which was cut short, in all their cases).<br /> <br /> Maybe if they weren't at the top of the power scale. Or maybe if they could somehow downgrade (an Abyssal shrugging off the curse - and Exaltation), yet maybe running around as a Heroic mortal or Half-Caste or something. I dunno. <br /> <br /> Maybe if they actually <i><b>gave something up</b></i> to prove their allegiance, rather than merely wanting to &quot;swap for better charms&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T10:38:01-08:00","id":410301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410246#post410246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there probably don't need to be rules for it, because that makes it feel a bit too immediate, and the rules never really gave you that much you couldn't get from common sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I criticize &quot;redemption&quot; (since they're so often favored by Mary Sue types), I'm on the opposite end with this.<br /> <br /> The aforementioned scenario <b>worked</b> because they gave us a solid mechanical way to express what was happening. It was awesome.<br /> <br /> There was <b>three</b> other variant scenarios - one of which involved Caine, social combat and him accepting his fault. <i><b>It kind of sucked</b></i>. Great idea. But how do you execute it? <br /> <br /> It wasn't until <b>Glories of the First High - the Unconquered Sun</b>that we got that <b>awesome</b> charm expressing how Sol is basically invincible unless he fails a Virtue (I think it's Temperance?) ........ so <b>a decade</b> after Vampire <b>ended</b>, I read this <i>lovely</i> mechanical expression of a narrative goal (swapping Temperance for Conviction, you got Caine).<br /> <br /> Get me?<br /> <br /> Mechanics can be <i><b>beautiful </b></i>- and for those leery of &quot;hand wavium&quot;, they help us feel we're on the right track.<br /> <br /> And for where my criticism is focused (Mary Sues), <b>mechanical costs</b> can help weed them out. Even when it comes to Devil-Tigers (who wanted to emulate Solar themes), I <b>always</b> felt that they had a strong tendency to forget to include flaws or distortions --- they just add power and glory and whateverthefuck. <b>Mechanics</b> make costs &quot;concrete&quot;. Scary the wary away, the uncommitted, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T10:44:03-08:00","id":410313,"title":"","content":"I think that if Abyssal Redemption is a thing, Solar Corruption should also be a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T10:46:17-08:00","id":410315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410245#post410245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think that word means what you think it does. I see pattern recognition, but not proof of theme. What is being discussed here is a motif, not a theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>I checked a dictionary. It does mean what I think it means.<br /> <br /> What people are objecting to is how the Redemption narrative for Abyssals relate to the theme of Solars, this being: &quot;the consequences of the use of power&quot;, and how it just assumes that any an all uses of Solar power are morally superior to Abyssal power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410245#post410245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the &quot;theme&quot; of the Solars is almost meaningless to individual Solars. Similarly, characters in Creation have ideas about what constitutes good and evil, regardless of what the truth is, because they aren't being written from a meta standpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by this argument your comment makes even less sense. If splat theme makes little difference for individual Exalts and they are guided by their own in character moral compass... Why would they want to become part of the Evil Solar Anathema? And what does it matter how good or evil individual Solars are presented in the books? It isn't like any random Abyssal has access to their writeups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","user":"Ravraxas","date":". 02-18-2015, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T10:52:48-08:00","id":410323,"title":"","content":"I think we're looking at abyssal redemption backwards. Shiny and Golden is the shard's natural state. If you start acting too much like a solar, it's going to force it's way back to normal whether you want it to or not. <br /> <br /> Which opens up the possibility of an abyssal fighting to keep their exaltation nice and black while it tries to go all sunny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T11:01:44-08:00","id":410333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410323#post410323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we're looking at abyssal redemption backwards. Shiny and Golden is the shard's natural state. If you start acting too much like a solar, it's going to force it's way back to normal whether you want it to or not.<br /> <br /> Which opens up the possibility of an abyssal fighting to keep their exaltation nice and black while it tries to go all sunny.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what &quot;acting like a Solar&quot; is supposed to be? Acting like a grand and magnificent mythical hero? because if so there are not going to be Abyssals left withing a week.<br /> <br /> Solars are supposed to be the &quot;standard&quot; splat. The one that is capable of having all the breadth of human heroism withing itself. I don't think that &quot;acting like a Solar&quot; is a thing that its supposed to make any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T11:05:36-08:00","id":410335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410323#post410323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we're looking at abyssal redemption backwards. Shiny and Golden is the shard's natural state. If you start acting too much like a solar, it's going to force it's way back to normal whether you want it to or not.<br /> <br /> Which opens up the possibility of an abyssal fighting to keep their exaltation nice and black while it tries to go all sunny.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the shard was, through whatever means, changed. Nothing says it can't be changed back, or ever again. The possibility of redemption (or cleansing or whatever, since it is a <i>taint</i>) is just a logical outcrop of &quot;fix it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T12:30:24-08:00","id":410440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410333#post410333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what &quot;acting like a Solar&quot; is supposed to be? Acting like a grand and magnificent mythical hero? because if so there are not going to be Abyssals left withing a week.<br /> <br /> Solars are supposed to be the &quot;standard&quot; splat. The one that is capable of having all the breadth of human heroism withing itself. I don't think that &quot;acting like a Solar&quot; is a thing that its supposed to make any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difficulty in figuring out what that means is why it's so hard to do. Hence by Murphy's law it's going to be stumbled upon by an abyssal who wants nothing to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T12:42:42-08:00","id":410444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410440#post410440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difficulty in figuring out what that means is why it's so hard to do. Hence by Murphy's law it's going to be stumbled upon by an abyssal who wants nothing to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal champions the dead, spreads ancestor cults -- even finds a way to harmoniously stabilize them, ensuring that the ancestors educate and civilize and guide their barbarian descendants (and to hell with the corrupt gods of Yu Shan).<br /> <br /> When the Wyld threatens to flood into patches of Creation, thereby eradicating the shadowland-image of the area? The Abyssal uses necrotic might to kill the Fair Folk and forbid their passage.<br /> <br /> When the Yozis conspire to bring Creation under, such that it would desecrate the memory of the long departed? The Abyssal slays the fallen Primordial, sending it to join the Neverborn, and giving a clear signal to the rest of hell's prisoners.<br /> <br /> And then she begins glowing gold one day.<br /> <br /> And hates it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:17:17-08:00","id":410491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what &quot;acting like a Solar&quot; is supposed to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have phrased it as &quot;acting how the Unconquered Sun would prefer Solars to act, upholding his Virtues and preforming to a standard of heroism that he endorses.&quot; Your Exaltation shard presumably loves it when you do that, since that is what it is was made to do. I'd argue that acting like that has a real high chance of eventually making your shard start acting as it was originally conceived to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410444#post410444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssal champions the dead, spreads ancestor cults -- even finds a way to harmoniously stabilize them, ensuring that the ancestors educate and civilize and guide their barbarian descendants</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Spreading ancestor cults&quot; is inconsistent with &quot;harmoniously stabilizes them&quot;, because harmoniously stable ghosts <i>stop being ghosts.</i> They enter Lethe and are reborn. Being a ghost is a twisted, messed-up existence even for the best-adjusted among them, and every single ghost contributes to Oblivion merely by existing. The whole reason we have Oblivion is because there are a bunch of ghosts out there that <i>can't</i> ever enter Lethe.<br /> <br /> I keep seeing people either act like being a ghost is just like being a person. It is not. And I would argue it shouldn't be. If you can be a ghost without being psychologically damaged in some way that fetters you to a never-intended and very uncomfortable existence, then where is the downside to dying? You just became functionally immortal! Sure, you have to go live in the Underworld, but that's a small price to pay for continued existence that's just as comfortable as your previous one was. Very few people would want to enter Lethe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the Yozis conspire to bring Creation under, such that it would desecrate the memory of the long departed? The Abyssal slays the fallen Primordial, sending it to join the Neverborn, and giving a clear signal to the rest of hell's prisoners. </div> </div> </div>That's not a very good move if there were any other options, as she just made the most destructive things in the setting that much stronger and more powerful. There might be unintended side effects. The Labyrinth might suddenly grow immensely overnight and swallow half of Stygia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And then she begins glowing gold one day.<br /> <br /> And hates it. </div> </div> </div>Well, under 2e rules becoming a Solar would be a manifest upgrade, as suddenly she wouldn't have Resonance fucking up her life any more; limit is a lot more manageable. The only downside would be needing to start carrying Hearthstones to respire in the Underworld. <br /> <br /> She might not want to be a Solar, but, well, she signed up to murder the world and then went backsies on it. There are consequences for that sometimes.<br /> <br /> I have to admit that I am consistently baffled as to what precisely people who don't currently like them want from Abyssals. Their underlying design has been pretty consistent for two editions: the Neverborn made them to fulfill their aeons-long goal of ending everything. They can either embrace that, or rebel against it in some way, and <i>how they make that choice</i> and <i>deal withthe consequences </i>that come with it are the basis of how games involving Abyssal protagonists are supposed to evolve. If you aren't down with that, that's fine, but you have to make a case that that structure is just kind of inherently bad and wrong from a playability standpoint.<br /> <br /> It seems like a very big part of the underlying structure of their design is that there are big, big consequences for going back on your deal with the Neverborn. (I keep trying to type Malfeans, because I like the word Malfeans, even though I know we don't call them that anymore.) If you take that away, and take away anything at all resembling Resonance, aren't you basically just left with Solars that glow black? Solars as a splat have a kind of absolute freedom, because the Unconquered Sun doesn't compel them to do jack shit and they don't have day jobs (Sidereals) or existing societies imposing their own expectations on them (Lunars, Dragon-Blooded) and so can be whatever they want to be with no downside other than the fact that the world, in general, may not like them for it. Other splats don't get that, and that's okay. Some splats might wrap your character in heavy chains, because the point of them is interacting with those chains, and that is also okay.<br /> <br /> I mean, don't get me wrong, there's conceptual space for some kind of weird elegiac death-inflected Exalt who is suffused with the Underworld without necessarily being tied up in the whole Oblivion thing... but aren't Liminals going to be filling that niche?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:19:33-08:00","id":410493,"title":"","content":"I think my big problem with the redemption arc is you don't redeem types of people, you redeem your actions in the view of the one your seeking redemption from.<br /> <br /> In the angle of Abyssals to Solars I guess this makes sense, if you get the UCS approval he can turn you back into what is fitting for you to be in his eyes.<br /> <br /> But if you're an Abyssal who likes what they are, I can see you thinking that transformation is pretty terrible. Even if Abyssals can become Solars, there's nothing saying that makes them objectively moral superior in a numinous sense (partially because such a state is unknowable).<br /> <br /> Turning from Abyssal to Solar is only a statement about morality if it is impossible to act in a subjectively moral way as an Abyssal.<br /> <br /> And if the answer to that question is &quot;they can, but they still poison and doom the world by their very existence&quot; or even just &quot;they can, but only by murder&quot; then I feel like I've lost something that I really looked forward to playing in Third edition. <br /> <br /> I mean, I would be sad If the fact that you need to be able to play Vampire Hunter D (an idea I support) means that no one can play Abyssal who can create a lasting common good.<br /> <br /> Notice, please, that I am using &quot;create a good&quot; in the political and not in the moral sense. I mean an Abyssal Barrow Lord who genuinely cares for his buried principalities and whose subjects feel that their afterlives (heh) are enriched by his actions.<br /> <br /> Summed up, I'd like to feel that playing an Abyssal is not an exercise in futility if I'm not trying to turn into a solar or kill all-the-everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:27:48-08:00","id":410500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410313#post410313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that if Abyssal Redemption is a thing, Solar Corruption should also be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given a Deathlord can stick a Solar in a Monstrance and get an Abyssal out with work, I'd say it already <i>is</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:54:50-08:00","id":410515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410491#post410491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Spreading ancestor cults&quot; is inconsistent with &quot;harmoniously stabilizes them&quot;, because harmoniously stable ghosts <i>stop being ghosts.</i> They enter Lethe and are reborn. Being a ghost is a twisted, messed-up existence even for the best-adjusted among them, and every single ghost contributes to Oblivion merely by existing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.<br /> <br /> Plenty of people go to shit life-sucking jobs every day until they die.<br /> Many ghosts - especially Contagion ones - are just doing the same thing they've always done.<br /> Humans are inherently &quot;broken&quot; if you think the slightest neurosis makes us all crazy.<br /> <br /> Many ghost simply didn't want to give up life. It's that simple. In the comics there's even one of a human female who was hung as part of a witch hunt -- the text suggests that Mara (a demon) spread lies so as to have her removed (and then infiltrate, even taking her husband). The ghost is about to reincarnate.... until she gets pissed and realizes &quot;what a second - what the fuck - why enter Lethe when my village fucking <b>needs</b> me <i>more than ever</i> because there's a <b>demon</b> wreaking havoc with lies amongst them?&quot;<br /> <br /> So she returns as a ghost to help her village.<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> You can't presume Lethe fits everyone's personality. Hell, <i>given the option</i>, I rather spend a few centuries wreaking havoc on Earth than <b>ever</b> facing Lethe. I would need to <i>want to die </i>to accept Lethe. There's nothing good in it. I'm <i>not</i> a Buddhist nor a Hindu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410491#post410491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a very good move if there were any other options, as she just made the most destructive things in the setting that much stronger and more powerful. There might be unintended side effects. The Labyrinth might suddenly grow immensely overnight and swallow half of Stygia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly conjecture (half of which is absurd). The Neverborn aren't more powerful than the Yozis - they're crippled and ruined and progressively withering. The <i>best</i> they could produce - the Deathlords - are made from the tattered remains of their souls....the Yozi still have dozens upon dozens upon dozens and form entire world-bodies. The Yozis knew how to corrupt Solar Exaltations - the Neverborn aped the process, as best they could, creating gothic-Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410491#post410491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She might not want to be a Solar, but, well, she signed up to murder the world and then went backsies on it. There are consequences for that sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said backsies?<br /> <br /> Replace the gods with ghost cults. Murder a Yozi. Slaughter the Fair Folk. Murder is murder.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T14:30:26-08:00","id":410535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410515#post410515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Neverborn aren't more powerful than the Yozis</div> </div> </div> </div>They're in the odd position that they <i>have</i> more power, having taken the full might of a primordial with them when they died, but are unable to <i>use </i>it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T14:32:07-08:00","id":410538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410491#post410491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would have phrased it as &quot;acting how the Unconquered Sun would prefer Solars to act, upholding his Virtues and preforming to a standard of heroism that he endorses.&quot; Your Exaltation shard presumably loves it when you do that, since that is what it is was made to do. I'd argue that acting like that has a real high chance of eventually making your shard start acting as it was originally conceived to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Upholding Virtues that no longer exists on behalf of a god whose personality is supposed to be left up to the Storyteller? I don't think so.<br /> <br /> I assure you that in my games &quot;how the Unconquered Sun would prefer Solars to act&quot; is something supremely easy to do. Its something along the lines of &quot;To leave me alone to play the Games of Divinity&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, if you still live in 2e land... the Solars, as all other Exalted, were made to kill Primordials not to act however their patron wanted. In fact I seem to recall something about that being explicitly against their specifications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","user":"Ravraxas","date":". 02-18-2015, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T14:38:38-08:00","id":410543,"title":"","content":"Not &quot;how he wants&quot;. More &quot;In a way that strongly resonates with his nature&quot;. And especially &quot;not under the thumb of a bunch of ghosts&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T15:49:45-08:00","id":410657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410500#post410500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given a Deathlord can stick a Solar in a Monstrance and get an Abyssal out with work, I'd say it already <i>is</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what I meant. If that can be considered a valid &quot;Solar Corruption&quot; then the process of &quot;Abyssal Redemption&quot; needs only be the casting of a single Solar Sorcery spell.<br /> <br /> If Abyssal's &quot;redeem&quot; themselves into Solars by rebelling against their status as &quot;Exalted of Murder&quot;, then Solars should &quot;corrupt&quot; themselves if they embrace the status of &quot;Exalted of Murder&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T16:33:19-08:00","id":410725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410515#post410515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the setting says you are wrong. Existing as a ghost within the context of Creation makes you a broken thing-which-should-not-be, and it is also explicit that you have to be damaged for that to happen, and that a ghost is a fundamentally warped thing and no matter what a ghost is contributing to Oblivion by choosing to cling to a warped existence instead of entering the cycle of rebirth. Every single ghost is a potential Nephwrack, and the Neverborn whisper to all of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Strictly conjecture (half of which is absurd). The Neverborn aren't more powerful than the Yozis </div> </div> </div>They're not, no. It's a good thing I didn't say they were!<br /> <br /> The Neverborn want to destroy everything. This makes them a more destructive force than the Yozi's are, as the Yozi's want to rule the world, not kill it. There would be a slender thread of hope if the Yozi's reclaimed their thrones. There is no such hope if Creation falls into the void.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who said backsies? </div> </div> </div>... your hypothetical heroic Abyssal? She's creating structures and institutions designed to last, to perpetuate themselves. The Neverborn don't like that, because they want everything to end.<br /> <br /> Unless she's simply engaged in a long-term plan to very slowly subvert all of Creation to her ancestor cult, morph it gradually into a death cult, and then morph that death cult into a void cult.<br /> <br /> In which case, she is awesome and playing a super-long game with a high payoff.<br /> <br /> You are right that in such a situation she'd be very pissed off she turned into a Solar, but in such a situation she probably wouldn't turn into a Solar because she's still trying to murder everything, and that isn't really something I think would equate very well with suddenly turning into a golden god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T16:53:14-08:00","id":410761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410493#post410493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Summed up, I'd like to feel that playing an Abyssal is not an exercise in futility if I'm not trying to turn into a solar or kill all-the-everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, please, thank you. Abyssal narrative space has been really, really narrow for a long time and the result is that it's very predictable and boring, even with the vagaries and idiosyncrasies of different games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410323#post410323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shiny and Golden is the shard's natural state. If you start acting too much like a solar, it's going to force it's way back to normal whether you want it to or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is functionally meaningless. Solar Exaltation is amoral. It's a power that wants to be wielded, but cares not about the ends that power is put toward. Even if the Unconquered Sun personally Chooses his Chosen...even in the best-scenario portrayal of 3e characters, where most Solars are not lone wolf assholes incapable of forming true emotional attachments as 2e portrayed just about everyone, there are going to be some Solars who are just not nice people but who have an incredible drive that makes UCS take notice, who want to conquer the world and rule it from atop a throne of enslaved, oiled-up bodybuilders and take the head of anyone who speaks their name in an uneven tone. Such a character is definitely still a Solar!<br /> <br /> I mean, shit, look at the mythic inspirations for Solars. One and all, they are great and terrible figures. They are moody. They are casually murderous. They place themselves above humanity, because they are objectively greater than mortal humans and thereby do not consider themselves bound by the same social rules. They're not all LG Paladins!<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410444#post410444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssal champions the dead, spreads ancestor cults -- even finds a way to harmoniously stabilize them, ensuring that the ancestors educate and civilize and guide their barbarian descendants (and to hell with the corrupt gods of Yu Shan).<br /> <br /> When the Wyld threatens to flood into patches of Creation, thereby eradicating the shadowland-image of the area? The Abyssal uses necrotic might to kill the Fair Folk and forbid their passage.<br /> <br /> When the Yozis conspire to bring Creation under, such that it would desecrate the memory of the long departed? The Abyssal slays the fallen Primordial, sending it to join the Neverborn, and giving a clear signal to the rest of hell's prisoners.<br /> <br /> And then she begins glowing gold one day.<br /> <br /> And hates it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean this is an interesting idea but any ST who up and did this to a player as a CONSEQUENTIAL TWEEST would be a douchebag of the highest caliber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T17:27:56-08:00","id":410834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410725#post410725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the setting says you are wrong. Existing as a ghost within the context of Creation makes you a broken thing-which-should-not-be, and it is also explicit that you have to be damaged for that to happen, and that a ghost is a fundamentally warped thing and no matter what a ghost is contributing to Oblivion by choosing to cling to a warped existence instead of entering the cycle of rebirth. Every single ghost is a potential Nephwrack, and the Neverborn whisper to all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I'm getting here is that it is very much necessary to change this part of the setting. Because these things are utterly terrible for Exalted as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T17:53:44-08:00","id":410853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410725#post410725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And the setting says you are wrong. Existing as a ghost within the context of Creation makes you a broken thing-which-should-not-be, and it is also explicit that you have to be damaged for that to happen, and that a ghost is a fundamentally warped thing and no matter what a ghost is contributing to Oblivion by choosing to cling to a warped existence instead of entering the cycle of rebirth. Every single ghost is a potential Nephwrack, and the Neverborn whisper to all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I'm pretty sure that Exalted goes out of its way not to label anything as objectively &quot;a broken thing-which-should-not-be&quot;. Which book, exactly, are you getting this from? <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> hypothetical heroic Abyssal</div> </div> </div> </div>It's always been head-cannon of mine that if there is a way to usher the Neverborn to sleep, and possibly back onto whatever next steps awaits a dying Titan, an Abyssal is going to do it. And they'll do it in a way that isn't about murder, but about reconciliation. <br /> <br /> To know that titanic entities exist beneath their metaphysical feet in impotent rage, that the murdered architects of the world dream in torment, and then do fuck-all nothing about it forever seems like the greatest crime of the Celestial Exalted. If anything needs &quot;redeemed&quot; it's the murder of the Primordials followed by the careless indifference of the old and content. Of course, I'm not saying Creation would be a better place for humans if a few Primordials had never kicked the bucket, but I am saying that violence has consequences. And that doing nothing about those consequences (or in the case of the Black Nadir Concordat, making it worse) is shirking your responsibility for the great violation of existence. <br /> <br /> Exalted supports this idea of diminishment of existence due to the cycle of violence, I rather hold out hope that a non-violent solution could help make Creation into something subjectively better.<br /> If an Abyssals, culled from the ranks of the hopeless an malicious, empowered to bring ruin to Creation, can become an agent of reconciliation that half-turn back the cycle of endless vengeance ... <br /> <br /> For me, that's a redemption story. To hell with whatever color he or she glows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T18:01:31-08:00","id":410860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410761#post410761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean this is an interesting idea but any ST who up and did this to a player as a CONSEQUENTIAL TWEEST would be a douchebag of the highest caliber.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ya know, your character's behavior has totally stopped matching the alignment on your character sheet. Let's go ahead and make some changes.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Aren't we playing Exalted?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T18:07:19-08:00","id":410862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410515#post410515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many ghost simply didn't want to give up life. It's that simple. In the comics there's even one of a human female who was hung as part of a witch hunt -- the text suggests that Mara (a demon) spread lies so as to have her removed (and then infiltrate, even taking her husband). The ghost is about to reincarnate.... until she gets pissed and realizes &quot;what a second - what the fuck - why enter Lethe when my village fucking <b>needs</b> me <i>more than ever</i> because there's a <b>demon</b> wreaking havoc with lies amongst them?&quot;<br /> <br /> So she returns as a ghost to help her village.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> Not all ghosts are fundamentally broken. Somewhere in either MoEP: Abyssals or Compass: Underworld there is a passage about the aftermath of the usurpation when all the dead Solars ended up in the underworld. Since death freed them of the Great Curse, they were able to realize that they'd become monsters. the revelation drove many to choose Lethe and erase themselves from existence, while others stuck around in an attempt to fix their mistakes (Including the founder of the Timeless Order of Manacle and Coin, if I recall correctly).<br /> <br /> Death and becoming ghosts sounds like it fixed some of them. Hell, the first chapter comic of Compass: Underworld is about a dead solar leading what is presumably his circle against an undead army and talkng about how &quot;Here at the end, I will become what I should have been all along&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Found it. Compass: Underworld. pg. 14-15","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":4172,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","user":"Marros56","date":". 02-18-2015, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T18:23:18-08:00","id":410873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marros56</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410862#post410862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all ghosts are fundamentally broken. Somewhere in either MoEP: Abyssals or Compass: Underworld there is a passage about the aftermath of the usurpation when all the dead Solars ended up in the underworld. Since death freed them of the Great Curse, they were able to realize that they'd become monsters. the revelation drove many to choose Lethe and erase themselves from existence, while others stuck around in an attempt to fix their mistakes (Including the founder of the Timeless Order of Manacle and Coin, if I recall correctly).</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting aside the &quot;freed from the Great Curse upon death and realized their mistakes&quot; thing,* the founder and still leader of the Timeless Order was <i>definitely</i> not one of those. He passed away during the First Age with a funeral of especially ridiculous grandiosity, including the last few living members of a Primordial-born race getting buried alive with him to serve as his prized slaves in the afterlife. Having decided that he hadn't brought quite enough misery to others in life, he founded the Timeless Order because he decided slaves were the only wealth worth having in death and, dammit, he was going to have the most.<br /> <br /> * I can't deny it gives me the warm fuzzies, but in spite of that, I've personally never been too keen on it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T18:35:39-08:00","id":410886,"title":"","content":"I actually find that particular line to be a really unfortunate piece of Solar whitewashing. It's very much a &quot;oh, if not for the Curse they would have been awesome rulers of everything&quot; sentiment, which I feel to be a really bad statement to make about Solar hegemony.<br /> <br /> But in regards to the thrust of this conversation, yes, I agree that it should be perfectly valid for ghosts to be capable of existing in a way that is not harmful to the living. Unnatural, certainly, but Creation's natural order isn't exactly one concerned with the well-being of its inhabitants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T19:18:00-08:00","id":410927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410886#post410886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually find that particular line to be a really unfortunate piece of Solar whitewashing. It's very much a &quot;oh, if not for the Curse they would have been awesome rulers of everything&quot; sentiment, which I feel to be a really bad statement to make about Solar hegemony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, though given most of the stuff out there seems to say &quot;all the Solars were assholes&quot; it's nice to have a point where i can say some of them did right by someone (a good portion of the underworld, in this case.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T20:21:45-08:00","id":410952,"title":"","content":"How exactly does one redeem a Solar? Do you need to bring them to a special place? What do you get for redeeming them...a microwave oven, maybe? Can you still redeem your Solar if they're defective or have signs of obvious wear, or will they be refused in that case? Can you just be refunded for your Solar instead?<br /> <br /> Burning questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T20:24:51-08:00","id":410957,"title":"","content":"I now have an image of the Wyld Hunt collecting dead Solars like carnival tickets and trading them in for cheap plastic toys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T20:33:15-08:00","id":410973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410952#post410952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly does one redeem a Solar? Do you need to bring them to a special place? What do you get for redeeming them...a microwave oven, maybe? Can you still redeem your Solar if they're defective or have signs of obvious wear, or will they be refused in that case? Can you just be refunded for your Solar instead?<br /> <br /> Burning questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, see, when you got your Solar, you paid an extra 5 obols to your local Satrapy as part of the purchase price. When you're done with your Solar, you can bring them to any redemption center to get your 5 obols back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T22:22:00-08:00","id":411070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410725#post410725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the setting says you are wrong. Existing as a ghost within the context of Creation makes you a broken thing-which-should-not-be, and it is also explicit that you have to be damaged for that to happen, and that a ghost is a fundamentally warped thing and no matter what a ghost is contributing to Oblivion by choosing to cling to a warped existence instead of entering the cycle of rebirth. Every single ghost is a potential Nephwrack, and the Neverborn whisper to all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're conflating very different things.<br /> <br /> Yes, from the perspective of Yu Shan and the Heavens and all that shit, Ghosts are broken.<br /> <br /> No, from the perspective of Ancestor Cults, your great-great-grandmother teaching you the medicine she mastered over decades, to help you heal her descendants is not broken.<br /> <br /> Yes, in the grand scheme of things, someone probably cares about them maybe becoming Nephwracks.<br /> <br /> No, in anyones personal narrative, there are a thousand reasons why it's far more sensible to stick around with your loved ones than go to Lethe.<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> As my example depicted, there are ghosts - in the books - who stuck around <i>to fight demons</i> and <i>help their people</i>, because everyone knows Yu Shan isn't doing a shit about it.<br /> <br /> As others have said, there are ghosts - in the books - once Solars, who realized they were <i>broken</i> in life and now - cleansed by death - persisted as heroes against the Void. It was the <i>broken</i> ones who were either too selfish or too vain to accept their new existence and remedy some of their wrongs (instead opting for the easy way out, via Lethe, to get recycled). For all you know, they were immediately reborn as farmers who died in the Contagion - same soul, just much less wise, powerful or useful. Ha.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410725#post410725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not, no. It's a good thing I didn't say they were!<br /> <br /> The Neverborn want to destroy everything. This makes them a more destructive force than the Yozi's are, as the Yozi's want to rule the world, not kill it. There would be a slender thread of hope if the Yozi's reclaimed their thrones. There is no such hope if Creation falls into the void.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive me, but it seem to have been implied, when you suggested that killing a Yozi made things worse.<br /> <br /> Also, I think it's worth noting that the books also posit the possibility of the Abyssal Exalted being capable of ending <i>even them</i> (or at least mutilating so much further, like grinding up meat so you can flush it down the drain). Since the whole example was predicated on an Abyssal who could solo a Yozi, I'll wager the same Abyssal could continue cutting up the freshly-created Neverborn (who probably will need time adjusting to their new state of being anyways). In the 1E Autochtonian scenarios, one of them <b>explicitly</b> covered the possibility of Autochton's death (possibly even deliberate, accelerated by the First and Forsaken Lion) -- and not only would a Neverborn be inferior (and increasingly weaker) compared to their living version, but <i>a Deathlord</i> basically turns the freshly turned Neverborn into <i>a fancy mount</i>, using Autochtonia to wage war against the other Neverborn.<br /> <br /> TLDR: An Abyssal could probably snuff a Yozi's Fetich and then proceed to slice up any and all subsequent souls. Nothing dictates that the Abyssal must stop at some point, meaning it could keep slicing until the newly minted Neverborn is a wreck. I'd even be somewhat fitting to see the Neverborn have created something more horrific than the Solar Exalted who murdered them. It's lovely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410725#post410725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... your hypothetical heroic Abyssal? She's creating structures and institutions designed to last, to perpetuate themselves. The Neverborn don't like that, because they want everything to end.<br /> <br /> Unless she's simply engaged in a long-term plan to very slowly subvert all of Creation to her ancestor cult, morph it gradually into a death cult, and then morph that death cult into a void cult.<br /> <br /> In which case, she is awesome and playing a super-long game with a high payoff.<br /> <br /> You are right that in such a situation she'd be very pissed off she turned into a Solar, but in such a situation she probably wouldn't turn into a Solar because she's still trying to murder everything, and that isn't really something I think would equate very well with suddenly turning into a golden god.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are all different things.<br /> <br /> Fuck what the Neverborn like --- no matter how displeased they are, they'd <b>never</b> want one of their Abyssals to go Solar just because they're &quot;misguided&quot; and spreading ancestor cults.<br /> <br /> And on the same point, this heroic Abyssal could totally disregard the Neverborn - and sincerely venerate the dead. <b>There is a canon Abyssal</b> in the books who is an example of this, teaching mortals how to venerate their ancestors - and punishing ghosts who don't honor their prayers. <br /> <br /> It's not binary.<br /> <br /> People don't have to be &quot;I WILL DESTROY THE WORLD&quot; or else &quot;I LOVE THE WORLD AND WISH TO BE PURE&quot;. There are a lot of in-betweens, even full of contradictions, but firmly <b>away</b> from the extremes.<br /> .<br /> <br /> Hell, Infernals were created for the Reclamation -- but I quickly grew disinterested because I <i>loathe</i> the Ebon Dragon. <br /> <br /> But if my ST said &quot;ah-ha! you hate the Ebon Dragon and oppose the Reclamation! Redemption is within your grasp!&quot;, I'd snuff out the sun myself until I quit glowing gold. Or I'd use those Solar charms (they have a ton of Creature-of-Darkness and Divine Judgement style ones) to send entire cities to Malfeas, to curse the gods, and to use Holy-seduction combos to brow-beat the Yozis into helping me fuck up Yu Shan.<br /> <br /> Because fuck that oversimplified binary shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T23:35:14-08:00","id":411132,"title":"","content":"Abyssal Redemption isn't about good vs evil, it's about life vs death.<br /> <br /> When an Abyssal becomes a Solar, they cease to be a Creature of the Underworld (and a Creature of Darkness), and become a being of Creation once again, a being who is no longer despised by the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> Redemption is more about being &quot;redeemed&quot; in the eyes of the Unconquered Sun, and about deciding that Life is more important than Death, than anything having to do with morality.<br /> <br /> And yeah, any ST who forces the player who liked his Abyssal to instead be a Solar is a jerk. But that's on the ST, not on the basic concept of Redemption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T02:29:35-08:00","id":411233,"title":"","content":"The thing to remember is that Redemption doesn't necessarily have anything to do with redemption. You could actually end up a worse person after the fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T06:25:29-08:00","id":411409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=411233#post411233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing to remember is that Redemption doesn't necessarily have anything to do with redemption. You could actually end up a worse person after the fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>If so, then calling it &quot;Redemption&quot; is needlessly confusing. &quot;Redemption&quot; has very specific moral connotations.<br /> <br /> I'm in the &quot;Redemption as written needlessly limits Abyssal concept-space&quot; camp. Even if you assume that Redeeming an Abyssal Exalt has no implications at all for the Abyssal's personal morality, or that objective morality does not exist in the Exalted setting, you still have the basic problem that the game is forcing you to play your Abyssal a certain way, or you'll turn into another kind of Exalt.<br /> <br /> None of the other splats have this problem. Sidereals who go ronin get stripped of their heavenly job benefits, but they're still Sidereals. Lunars who won't join the Silver pact have an elevated risk of chimerism, but they're still Lunars. Dragonblooded who aren't noble are either outcaste or dead Dragonblooded. Alchemicals who develop Gremlin Syndrome are still Alchemicals, only crazy and armed with flesh-warping powers.<br /> <br /> Also, consider what Redemption does in tandem with Resonance. Every time an Abyssal resists unnnatural mental influence, channels a virtue, or commits &quot;any deed that actively promotes or defends life&quot;, he gains Resonance points, which can manifest a variety of destructive effects.<br /> <br /> The net effect is that any given Abyssal character can effectively only play one of three character arcs:<br /> 1. Omnicidal Nihilism - the Abyssal follows the script and murders everything. It can be challenging to do that without being a one-note character.<br /> 2. Defiance - the Abyssal goes off the script and gains Resonance like crazy but persists until eventually the Neverborn and the ST give up and say &quot;Fine, evidently you don't want to be an omnicidal nihilist. Here's a different character.&quot;<br /> 3. Enlightenment - the Abyssal 2E book mentions how an Abyssal might stay in the underworld and be a hero to the dead instead of the living, but provides no actual detail about how that would work, what that would mean, or how the ST is supposed to handle it.<br /> <br /> Based on what I have read of this thread, the people who are most disappointed in Abyssals are the people who are most interested in Enlightenment and wish the game provided more support for it, or wish for more possible arcs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 02-19-2015, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:06:29-08:00","id":411435,"title":"","content":"The difference there is that none of the other Exalted were made by deforming another type.<br /> <br /> I mean really, if you choose to play an abyssal, but then go &quot;But I'm not going to murder everything, that would be boring. Instead I'm going to fight for a just cause and be all heroic and shit&quot; aren't you <i>already</i> playing a solar? Redemption is just the game/ST going &quot;Yeah, you're not fooling anyone any more&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:11:07-08:00","id":411443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=411435#post411435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference there is that none of the other Exalted were made by deforming another type.<br /> <br /> I mean really, if you choose to play an abyssal, but then go &quot;But I'm not going to murder everything, that would be boring. Instead I'm going to fight for a just cause and be all heroic and shit&quot; aren't you <i>already</i> playing a solar? Redemption is just the game/ST going &quot;Yeah, you're not fooling anyone any more&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Infernals were made that way, and their narratives are nowhere near as thin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:15:46-08:00","id":411447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=411435#post411435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference there is that none of the other Exalted were made by deforming another type.<br /> <br /> I mean really, if you choose to play an abyssal, but then go &quot;But I'm not going to murder everything, that would be boring. Instead I'm going to fight for a just cause and be all heroic and shit&quot; aren't you <i>already</i> playing a solar? Redemption is just the game/ST going &quot;Yeah, you're not fooling anyone any more&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no you are not. You're playing an Abyssal who is also a hero, that does not make you a Solar. Or rather, it should not. Because that's stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:31:03-08:00","id":411460,"title":"","content":"If you're really playing a Heroic Abyssal there will be sufficient disparity between your actions and those of a solar with the same goals that redemption is not an issue. <br /> <br /> Basically if you can tell the difference, you ain't going gold. If you can't, then you were already redeemed before it got made official, and you did it to yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:32:35-08:00","id":411462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=411435#post411435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference there is that none of the other Exalted were made by deforming another type.<br /> <br /> I mean really, if you choose to play an abyssal, but then go &quot;But I'm not going to murder everything, that would be boring. Instead I'm going to fight for a just cause and be all heroic and shit&quot; aren't you <i>already</i> playing a solar? Redemption is just the game/ST going &quot;Yeah, you're not fooling anyone any more&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, because Solars don't always fight for a just cause and be heroic and shit. Some might, but you have plenty of others who are savage, conquering warlords who slaughter cities, or heartless assassins who kill for money, or lore seekers who would happy sacrifice thousands for some lost bit of knowledge. Solars are not Paladins and they don't always wear white hats.<br /> <br /> You can play a really nice Abyssal who goes around and helps people, and you won't have to worry about turning into a Solar. Because, &quot;being a nice person&quot; isn't what's needed for Redemption. It's seeking atonement from the Unconquered Sun and Creation itself, casting aside the underworld and becoming a champion of the living. That doesn't necessarily require being a saint.<br /> <br /> A cruel warlord who marches against the Underworld, closing Shadowlands and horrifically torturing ghosts until they finally submit to Lethe could certainly find the Unconquered Sun's favor and find himself turning into an Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:43:58-08:00","id":411468,"title":"","content":"As has been noted, it would help enormously if going from Abyssal to Solar wasn't a straight mechanical upgrade. Like, shedding your cursed power is less poignant if it's to become a god-king of everything with all the same powers you had before only better.<br /> <br /> If shedding your Abyssal status caused you to become a mortal, but the displays of heroism required to do such a thing were so grand that such a former Abyssal was exceedingly likely to then become a Solar the next time that they were in a situation where they might potentially be chosen, that would be much more resonant with these sorts of character arcs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:45:23-08:00","id":411470,"title":"","content":"That would kick the &quot;No Un-Exaltation&quot; rule straight in the nuts though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:51:49-08:00","id":411474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=411468#post411468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As has been noted, it would help enormously if going from Abyssal to Solar wasn't a straight mechanical upgrade. Like, shedding your cursed power is less poignant if it's to become a god-king of everything with all the same powers you had before only better.<br /> <br /> If shedding your Abyssal status caused you to become a mortal, but the displays of heroism required to do such a thing were so grand that such a former Abyssal was exceedingly likely to then become a Solar the next time that they were in a situation where they might potentially be chosen, that would be much more resonant with these sorts of character arcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's plenty of space there between &quot;not a mechanical upgrade&quot; but also &quot;still Exalted.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't really have a problem with Abyssals being CoDs, needing to wear certain trappings to respire non-Death Essence, etc. There probably should be some inherent benefit to that that is not tied to their being patronized by the Deathlords (though that infrastructural advantage is not to be ignored). Is drinking blood for Essence that advantage? Maybe - certainly, if you can't constantly stunt back motes then blood-drinking suddenly becomes a much more valuable power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T08:03:20-08:00","id":411569,"title":"","content":"Their max lifespan does suddenly get infinitely smaller. Aside from that I wonder if delving deeper into vampiric myths could be beneficial. Some sort of inherent resistance to damage or healing factor, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T08:19:02-08:00","id":411579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=411462#post411462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are not Paladins and they don't always wear white hats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, one of my character concepts I've been sitting on for Ex3 is a sorcerous con-artist Solar who uses his magic to disguise himself as Dragon-Blooded, so he can simultaneously evade the notice of the Wyld Hunt, foment unrest in the Tengese against the Realm, and most importantly, <i>abuse the shit out of</i> the horrible system of exploitation set in place by the Realm to enjoy its benefits. <br /> <br /> Because nice is nice, but hookers and blow in the howdah of a majestic elephant is <i>bitchin'</i>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\">I'm pretty certain I'd hate this guy IRL, but it'll be an interesting RP challenge.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T08:20:29-08:00","id":411582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=411569#post411569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their max lifespan does suddenly get infinitely smaller.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very much mostly an academic point. Most Exalts don't get the luxury of dying in old age, and didn't even in the First Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 02-19-2015, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T08:45:10-08:00","id":411613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=411582#post411582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is very much mostly an academic point. Most Exalts don't get the luxury of dying in old age, and didn't even in the First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. Plus, Solars can live for 10,000 years or so. I think in 2nd edition, the First Age lasted for something like 6000 years or so, and between the Shogunate and Second Age you have somewhere around 1500 years. So since the Primordial War only ~7500 years have passed. At year Zero, a Solar who had Exalted a millennium before the end of the Primordial War would still have another 1500 years in front of him.<br /> <br /> So for all practical purposes, Solars might as well be immortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T08:53:57-08:00","id":411625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=411613#post411613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for all practical purposes, Solars might as well be immortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Sidereals are the longest lived Exalts at 5000 years maximum. Solars top out at 3000 years.<br /> <br /> For game purposes, practically immortal applies to Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T09:31:51-08:00","id":411680,"title":"","content":"I think the first age only lasted about 4000 years. That was still enough time for a Solar to die of old age and spark a bit of a mass midlife crisis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T09:52:11-08:00","id":411698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=411625#post411625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Sidereals are the longest lived Exalts at 5000 years maximum. Solars top out at 3000 years.<br /> <br /> For game purposes, practically immortal applies to Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe there was some caveat that Solars and Lunars can find means of extending their lifespan, through which they can exceed Sidereals'. Meanwhile, Sidereals just don't have anything they can do about it.<br /> <br /> I have no idea if any of that will persist into the new edition. As it's not really necessary information for the vast, vast majority of games, I could see any specifics on lifespan being left unclear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T09:58:13-08:00","id":411704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=411435#post411435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference there is that none of the other Exalted were made by deforming another type.<br /> <br /> I mean really, if you choose to play an abyssal, but then go &quot;But I'm not going to murder everything, that would be boring. Instead I'm going to fight for a just cause and be all heroic and shit&quot; aren't you <i>already</i> playing a solar? Redemption is just the game/ST going &quot;Yeah, you're not fooling anyone any more&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if your ambitions are a little less grandiose or more self-serving than &quot;murder everything?&quot; What if you want to start your own vampire clan, or become the most powerful necromancer ever, or found a kingdom on the backs of thousands of zombie slaves, or murder <i>only those people over there</i> but don't care about Creation in general and are content to live and let live?<br /> <br /> Then either Resonance will screw you because you're &quot;defending life&quot; by protecting your land, people, or possessions, or you wander into that nebulous &quot;Enlightenment&quot; space that the developers didn't really plan for you to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T10:06:38-08:00","id":411709,"title":"","content":"You're not defending life if your people are undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T10:27:54-08:00","id":411742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=411709#post411709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not defending life if your people are undead.</div> </div> </div> </div>...then you've wandered into that nebulous &quot;Enlightenment&quot; space that the developers didn't really plan for you to go, which &quot;could change everything, even the game's basic assumptions.&quot; (MoEP: Abyssals 228). <br /> <br /> Seriously, this is what is written into the Storytelling section of the book. The three arcs are clearly labeled &quot;Path of Wickedness&quot;, &quot;Path of Defiance&quot;, and &quot;Path of Enlightenment&quot;. Guess which section is the shortest?<br /> <br /> Some other examples, more attuned to life:<br /> * You're attached to a particular community of living people who you were a part of before you Exalted. After you Exalt, you decide you want to help this community prosper, and you can't do that solely by murdering its enemies.<br /> * You want revenge on the people who killed you, and then after that you want to live a safe and easy existence full of love and creature comforts.<br /> * You accepted the Deathlord's pact because you were desperate, and now you want out. Killing your master would be great, but escape is also acceptable.<br /> * You only want to kill Wyld creatures, and other outsiders that threaten the Creation you're comfortable with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T10:35:12-08:00","id":411746,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Path of Enlightenment got the short end of the stick in 2nd edition. Morke and Holden have both already said that was problematic and that &quot;freelance Abyssals&quot; will get a fairer examination in 3rd edition, plus the Deathlords will be presented as less 2D black hat caricatures, so an Abyssal doesn't have to be a horrible, evil monster to want to work with them.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it was a problem, it was acknowledged as a problem, and presumably it won't be a problem from now on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T10:40:41-08:00","id":411752,"title":"","content":"To be fair, it's difficult to provide guidelines for &quot;pretty much whatever the fuck you want&quot;. It kinda comes under the same umbrella as vanilla exalted, but with a few obvious tweaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T17:03:21-08:00","id":412215,"title":"","content":"Controversial statement: saying redemption, and the idea of chafing under the Abyssal condition shouldn't exist is completely misunderstanding what the Abyssal feel IS, and actually insulting to it and reductive of them.<br /> <br /> *Puts on riot gear*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T20:10:33-08:00","id":412371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=412215#post412215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Controversial statement: saying redemption, and the idea of chafing under the Abyssal condition shouldn't exist is completely misunderstanding what the Abyssal feel IS, and actually insulting to it and reductive of them.<br /> <br /> *Puts on riot gear*</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course some Abyssals should be unhappy. They hunger for living flesh, thrive on pain and vice, are attended by creepy ghosts, and generally weird people out. Not everyone goes for that, even if they had some idea of what they were getting into. The problem is with the idea that redemption need be based on some kind of I-can't-believe-it's-not-alignment framework.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T08:49:27-08:00","id":412848,"title":"","content":"Haven't read the whole thread, but....<br /> <br /> In 3e, if I was gonna run Abyssal redemption and it made sense*<br /> <br /> I would *probably* be tempted to (unless the person wanted to redeem to be a Solar) run it as redemption not from Abyssal -&gt; Solar but as redemption from Abyssal to a Exigent that was aligned with ends and death and was not a Sidereal of the Endings Caste. (And I guess I wouldn't ask the player to give up power to do so.)<br /> <br /> Creation has many gods of death and darkness who are not of the Underworld yet wield power over it. They could make good patrons for a gothy Exalt who wasn't actually part of the Oblivion bringing gang.<br /> <br /> And that is a thing which can happen now.<br /> <br /> *on redemption: for me has teeth when people seeking redemption and restitution for wrongful, intention or negligent actions they have taken which have hurt others, not some nominal accepting of evil or tainted power, under duress, even if that comes with unintended consequences. that's the kind of thing any sane, morally reasonable person gives forgiveness out for without asking for redemption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T08:52:47-08:00","id":412850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409483#post409483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How irritating and stupid I find the incessant Redemption threads, mostly. In-setting, Solars aren't the thing people aspire to be, they're the bogeymen and monsters of myth.<br /> <br /> <br /> There is no objective standard of right, wrong, or evil in the setting. The Unconquered Sun is a glorified crack addict, the beings who created the world literally made mankind to suffer (and got stuffed into a box made of their own guts as repayment), the First Age Solars were monsters of such epic proportions that their loyal lieutenants and advisors dug up heroic willpower to resist their beyond-god-like power to influence the minds of others to brutally murder them all, and the current guys in charge of Creation haven't done so well either.<br /> <br /> On a metaphysical level, everyone is covered in shit and bad choices, and the good guys are those who are doing good things right now.<br /> <br /> If you want to redeem yourself for your bad choices in life, go forth and do good deeds. Wanting a little gold star for the effort is bloody *kindergarten* morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people (like my wife for example) REALLY enjoy kindergarten morality. And those stories should be available for those who wish to engage in them and thus, Solar Redemption arcs should be doable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T17:58:05-08:00","id":414672,"title":"","content":"I do think the Path of Enlightenment should totally be a supported thing for the Abyssals, separate from the Path of Redemption. I can see where some Abyssal players would want to play the Enlightenment thing without &quot;But Your Existence Inevitably Pushes Creation Into Oblivion's Maw!&quot; hanging over them. Can Abyssals then be Exalted of death and the Underworld, instead of Exalted of Oblivion? If Abyssals and Ghosts weren't inimical to Creation by their very existence that would actually reduce the grimdark, Creation Is Doomed feeling that I always got from 2E -- a possibility I hadn't thought about before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=411468#post411468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As has been noted, it would help enormously if going from Abyssal to Solar wasn't a straight mechanical upgrade. Like, shedding your cursed power is less poignant if it's to become a god-king of everything with all the same powers you had before only better.<br /> <br /> If shedding your Abyssal status caused you to become a mortal, but the displays of heroism required to do such a thing were so grand that such a former Abyssal was exceedingly likely to then become a Solar the next time that they were in a situation where they might potentially be chosen, that would be much more resonant with these sorts of character arcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were a ST, I would make Redemption a matter of reconciliation with Sol Invictus for sinning/blaspheming against him (accepting a stolen Exaltation, doing things he considers morally wrong, or that the character considers morally wrong, helping Oblivion) and wanting to reject death in favor of being an Exalt of Creation and life. That doesn't mean that their actions were morally wrong according to the player or ST's beliefs, let alone any objective measurement. It would be the choice of a character who does not want to be Abyssal, who decides being one was either wrong or just not what they want to be anymore, and tries to convince Sol, personally, to forgive them for the things that he sees as wrong in Abyssals, and adopt them as his Chosen.<br /> <br /> And if that Abyssal does become a Solar, yeah they lose whatever (hopefully less punitive) mechanic replaces Resonance, and they no longer have the Great Curse, which means their story is also a story of potentially redeeming the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> But the Sun also demands sacrifice, and the nature of turning their exaltation inside out forces sacrifice. Depending on the character arc and the circumstances leading up to the change, they might die, or lose a limb, or lose all their artifacts. At the very least, they are now almost a newly Exalted Solar. Their connection to the Underworld is washed away -- Essence back town to 2. Their powers of death are erased -- they lose all charms except up to 10 excellencies (or just 10 starting Solar charms if excellencies aren't a thing in 3E). Maybe they keep sorcerous initiations, but can't use them until they build their Solar Essence up to the pre-requisites. They lose all attunements to soulsteel artifacts and Abyssal manses. Their Abyssal heartstones shatter. Some of their Backgrounds are taken away. They aren't quite starting over, because they keep their Attributes, Abilities, Virtues, and some types of merits and artifacts. But they still lost a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 02-21-2015, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T23:47:27-08:00","id":414956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410163#post410163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Redemption doesn't make sense in 2e because every Solar was written as a banally evil fuckwit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really?<br /> <br /> REALLY?<br /> <br /> A lot of 2e canon Solars were good guys and gals. Always flawed, but team good? Yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, flipping it around and contextualising it, this post implies that Redemption will make sense in 3e because some/all Solars will *not* be written as banally evil fuckwits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Some? Already so.<br /> All? ALL Solars are good guys and girls out to save the world from wickedness and ruin?<br /> <br /> <br /> That ain't Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I'm ignoring &quot;banally&quot;, because I *really* don't see how it makes it better if some Solars are cartoonishly and/or ruthlessly evil)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Redemption didn't make sense for a lot of reasons, but the solution being to actually make Solars all be paragons of good and justice...<br /> <br /> <br /> ...actually, I'm sold. I'm quite happy being able to say &quot;no, that plan is wicked, and no Solar would think of such a thing&quot; to players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T14:32:47-08:00","id":415721,"title":"","content":"Coming back to this topic, I've changed my mind 'redemption' in the setting and re: Abyssals to Solars. My knee jerk reaction to hearing &quot;Abyssal redemption&quot; is also hearing &quot;abyssals are inherently bringing Creation closer to its inevitable end, and nothing but changing your label is ever going to change that&quot;.<br /> <br /> Given how the developers have said this isn't the case (I think? It's still way early in the game line, they might change their minds a half a dozen times) I can get on board with an Abyssal redeeming themselves in the eyes of the Unconquered Sun, acknowledging that <br /> <br /> 1) the Unconquered Sun's measurement of worthy is as subjective as any other fallible individual, and <br /> \u200b2) that your character is not, simply by existing, a toxic wound on the face of Creation that will inevitably drag it closer to Oblivion no matter what actions he or she takes.<br /> <br /> Not that anyone needs my approval =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T15:04:16-08:00","id":415738,"title":"","content":"I would totally be on-board with that.<br /> <br /> And even if the Sun demands repentence from an Abyssal (or Infernal) while offering Redemption as a carrot... a principled one can tell him to his face that he isn't good enough to be their god because he abandoned Creation, and they don't want his &quot;help&quot; making the world better!<br /> <br /> So yeah, maybe Cleansing is a better word than Redemption. Still, any Abyssal who wants to seek it likely does think of it as redeeming themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T18:08:43-08:00","id":415943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=415738#post415738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even if the Sun demands repentence from an Abyssal (or Infernal) while offering Redemption as a carrot... a principled one can tell him to his face that he isn't good enough to be their god because he abandoned Creation, and they don't want his &quot;help&quot; making the world better!</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily, the <b>only</b> time I wanted to be a Solar..... was for my most diabolical character concepts.<br /> The <b>only</b> thing I envy is the Holy keyword. It's great. Especially if you want to carve a retreat for yourself in Malfeas.<br /> <b>So as a Solar</b>, I have better charms for bludgeoning the demons and even Yozis before my golden-heeled feet.<br /> I can be a horrible tyrant, a blood-gorged queen or king - and it's <b>Holy</b> that would forever keep me above demon-kind.<br /> <br /> <b>Meanwhile, as an Infernal</b>, I have better charms for fixing Creation quickly and efficiently. But no Holy for keeping demons in line. :L","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T18:11:54-08:00","id":415946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=415943#post415943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Meanwhile, as an Infernal</b>, I have better charms for fixing Creation quickly and efficiently. But no Holy for keeping demons in line. :L</div> </div> </div> </div>Cecelyne stuff is competitive with Holy for keeping-in-line, if not for sheer killability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T06:30:18-08:00","id":416440,"title":"","content":"Back in 2E I was a perennial participant in threads like this one. The temptation is still there. But since we've heard that we can expect a profound change in the presentation of Abyssals in 3E, and we don't know anything but the broadest strokes of how it will change, it seems pointless to have this discussion for a long while yet. Wait until we know what Abyssals are like in 3E, and what they do. Until then you're just making assumptions and talking past each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T08:21:12-08:00","id":416503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=415946#post415946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cecelyne stuff is competitive with Holy for keeping-in-line, if not for sheer killability.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's good for subordinates, but not-so-much for punching above your weight class.<br /> <br /> I can use Solar Presence charms to make my social attacks UMI against Creatures of Darkness. <i>Doesn't matter</i> what Essence level or rank. Doesn't matter type. I can just spam it against Berengiere or Ligier or Malfeas and they've got nothing but a throbbing inkling feeling that whatever I'm saying <i>is right</i>.<br /> <br /> I can use the same charm (and couple with Ghost-Eating Technique) to <i>punch the pavement</i> in hell and inflict harm on Malfeas.<br /> <br /> Now given me Golden Janissary style. The ultimate charm. Notice how it's an AoE around the target demon? So I curbstomp <b>Malfeas</b> (the greatest demon ever) and <b>every other demon</b> within range of Malfeas begins glowing as holy fire consumes them. o_o<br /> <br /> More broken combos are likely possible.<br /> <br /> Plus I <b>hate</b> the Ebon Dragon. On principle. Cecelyne is no where near as rewarding with her charm kit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T10:19:50-08:00","id":416615,"title":"","content":"Unless your Essence is high enough for you to already be ridiculous in 2e, Malfeas' Hardness is going to render your attacks more or less moot. Not to mention the punch will likely shatter all the bones in your arm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T10:31:34-08:00","id":416636,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure Malf's perfect stands up to holy attacks anyway. And since he <i>is</i> a city...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:13:17-08:00","id":416693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=416503#post416503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's good for subordinates, but not-so-much for punching above your weight class.<br /> <br /> I can use Solar Presence charms to make my social attacks UMI against Creatures of Darkness. <i>Doesn't matter</i> what Essence level or rank. Doesn't matter type. I can just spam it against Berengiere or Ligier or Malfeas and they've got nothing but a throbbing inkling feeling that whatever I'm saying <i>is right</i>.<br /> <br /> I can use the same charm (and couple with Ghost-Eating Technique) to <i>punch the pavement</i> in hell and inflict harm on Malfeas.<br /> <br /> Now given me Golden Janissary style. The ultimate charm. Notice how it's an AoE around the target demon? So I curbstomp <b>Malfeas</b> (the greatest demon ever) and <b>every other demon</b> within range of Malfeas begins glowing as holy fire consumes them. o_o<br /> <br /> More broken combos are likely possible.<br /> <br /> Plus I <b>hate</b> the Ebon Dragon. On principle. Cecelyne is no where near as rewarding with her charm kit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have a large misunderstanding of Primodials/Yozi. Holy does more damage on Creatures of Darkness (CoD for because that's way more than I'd like to type repeatedly.) The thing is you're thinking of the Yozi in terms of person sized combat. If you punch the pavement with a holy charm then you eventually break the pavement as far as damage goes congrats you're, at best, a mosquito. If Malfeas decides you annoy him enough to take personal issue then the ground will snap up and grind you into paste, a building will fall on you, or the district goes up in Malfean fire. And all of that is predicated on a single solar being able to inflict enough damage to draw Malfeas' attention.<br /> Put simply if it were that easy to take a Yozi or Primordial then there wouldn't have been a primodial war. There wouldn't have been other exalt types because as you're saying Solars are the ones with the holy charms. If all you need to cow the Primordials or the Yozi is a charm with the Holy key word then there would have been no point in making other exalts since all that would have been needed is the solars.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:34:10-08:00","id":416700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=416693#post416693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you punch the pavement with a holy charm then you eventually break the pavement as far as damage goes congrats you're, at best, a mosquito.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've heard, if you punch the pavement with Ghost-Eating Technique, then you're actually supposed to be able to kill Malfeas if you hit it hard enough. The actual problem is that <i>this</i> pavement has Perfect Defenses, Perfect Attacks, and a <i>lot</i> more motes than even Elder Solars.<br /> <br /> I don't like it, but that's what I heard. Well, read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:15:45-08:00","id":416742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=416700#post416700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've heard, if you punch the pavement with Ghost-Eating Technique, then you're actually supposed to be able to kill Malfeas if you hit it hard enough. The actual problem is that <i>this</i> pavement has Perfect Defenses, Perfect Attacks, and a <i>lot</i> more motes than even Elder Solars.<br /> <br /> I don't like it, but that's what I heard. Well, read.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's speculation on the grounds that Ghost-Eating Technique says it can dissipate spirits if you remove its last health level. One of the books also stated that no way was ever going to be given for how to permanently kill a Yozi/Primodial,so the idea that punching Malfeas hard enough with Ghost-Eating Technique destroying him is just speculation and theory. It falls down to a table to table basis as opposed to an absolute rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T13:36:19-08:00","id":416845,"title":"","content":"Ghost-eating technique is but one ingredient of the neverbornification combo pie. It's the flour, but you still need some eggs and butter and filling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T14:19:35-08:00","id":416882,"title":"","content":"Didn't the 2nd edition core book specifically say that the Solars used Ghost Eating Technique to kill the Primordials?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T14:36:05-08:00","id":416893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=416882#post416882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't the 2nd edition core book specifically say that the Solars used Ghost Eating Technique to kill the Primordials?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but they never gave a direct method for doing so. <br /> <br /> Also, I mean, the book can say a lot in fluff text without really meaning for that to be interpreted as the be-all end-all of what is necessary.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T15:04:29-08:00","id":416918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=409508#post409508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pick a system of belief. Punch everyone who does something that disagrees with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Punch <b>any</b>one who does something that disagrees with it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T15:35:33-08:00","id":416929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=416742#post416742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One of the books also stated that no way was ever going to be given for how to permanently kill a Yozi/Primodial,.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never understood that reticence on the part of the Devs - your character has ALREADY killed Yozis in a past life! Say, &quot;Essence 10, combination of lost super charms, teamwork of all 300 Solars to do it&quot;, but don't say, &quot;Sorry, your character will never know how she did this amazing thing that canonically she did&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5154-cappadocius","name":"cappadocius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T16:05:13-08:00","id":416949,"title":"","content":"They don't give it you because you have to figure it out yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T17:08:19-08:00","id":416984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cappadocius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=416929#post416929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never understood that reticence on the part of the Devs - your character has ALREADY killed Yozis in a past life! Say, &quot;Essence 10, combination of lost super charms, teamwork of all 300 Solars to do it&quot;, but don't say, &quot;Sorry, your character will never know how she did this amazing thing that canonically she did&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well its not like exalts remember every detail of their previous lives, and the lives that were involved in the Primordial War aren't exactly your immediate predecessor, so details lost. Also its not like you're character's predecessor did it. You were just in an army that did it. I mean actually slain Primordials only number a little over one or two dozen if I recall, so it isn't like every single solar in the war managed to get the kill shot on a primordial. It also falls firmly into the &quot;If you stat it, they will kill it&quot; rule of games. The point of the game isn't supposed to be going off and slaughtering the Yozi. If you and your group want to then alright that's your campaign goal, but that doesn't necessitate official methods for killing the Yozi/Primordials. Plus if you give a definite answer then you know you're going to have the one guy who looked it up and then argues that his character totally knows how because he has lore 5. Finally it also just kills more stories than it makes. I mean the primordials are worlds unto themselves even as Yozi they still have a tendency to be described as infinite in size. They are conceptual beings. Far more fun to allow the STs the option of saying &quot;Alright Malfeas is the king of all Yozi, he is literally the concept of the king meaning the only way to kill him is through conquest and claiming his throne.&quot; or if you're being silly Malfeas being king means he can only be killed by convincing the other Yozi to form a democratic government. Or Malfeas is the Demon City made of bronze so you need to basically melt the city to a puddle to kill him, or you need to slay his third circles in a 12 hour period and cap it off by ripping the city apart and slaying any humaniform jouten he has outside of a city. If you list down the specific combo needed to kill a Yozi you lose the fun of coming up with those ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T18:16:08-08:00","id":417031,"title":"","content":"I completely agree with you nalak, except the part about past lives. We know that Arianna's past life (Bright Shattered Ice?), and the first Solar queen (Merela?) both participated in the Primordial War, each was credited with killing a Primordial, and both died in the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> I'm against giving concrete ways to kill Primordials. In addition to everything nalak said, each Primordial is unique. Killing one should always be unique and specific to that particular Primordial, not just a matter of combining charms X, Y, and Z in the correct order and spamming the B button. Making a formula that's the same for each one turns something mythical and special into just another mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 02-23-2015, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T18:38:30-08:00","id":417043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=417031#post417031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely agree with you nalak, except the part about past lives. We know that the signature Twilight's past life (Shattered Ice Something?), and the first queen (Merela?) both participated in the Primordial War, each was credited with killing a Primordial, and both died in the Usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I don't recall mention of them being survivors of the Primordial war. Merela (or however her name is spelled) I recall has the deathblow on a Primordial. I don't recall Shattered Ice having that credit as well let alone them surviving from the war to the Usurpation. Interesting to know I might be able to play with that in campaign I'm running. Though I'm guessing those two would be exceptions rather than the rule.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T19:07:39-08:00","id":417055,"title":"","content":"According to Lords of Creation page 34 there were 12 Solars who survived from the Primordial War to the Era of Dreams.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T19:19:09-08:00","id":417077,"title":"","content":"I think some author or dev even mentioned that Merela was &quot;unceremoniously ganked&quot; because she wasn't actually as unbelievably amazing as everyone assumed. Bright Shattered Ice killed something which may have been a Primordial, or a Third Circle Soul, or a Behemoth. Hunanura, the Heart-Frost Unending, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 02-24-2015, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T19:51:03-08:00","id":417097,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I'll admit I didn't read too much of the first age books. Didn't really interest me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T23:18:10-08:00","id":417279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=416893#post416893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but they never gave a direct method for doing so.<br /> <br /> Also, I mean, the book can say a lot in fluff text without really meaning for that to be interpreted as the be-all end-all of what is necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand. The rules for Ghost Eating Technique are pretty clear (remove a spirit's last health level while using the Charm and it activates). And the charm says it was used to slay the Neverborn. So it seems clear that using Ghost Eating Technique while killing a Primordial will turn it into a Neverborn.<br /> <br /> I don't follow the logic of turning it an Air Breathing Mermaid situation where the Solars needed 4 or 5 other Charms to perma-kill a Primordial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T23:59:13-08:00","id":417298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=417279#post417279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't understand. The rules for Ghost Eating Technique are pretty clear (remove a spirit's last health level while using the Charm and it activates). And the charm says it was used to slay the Neverborn. So it seems clear that using Ghost Eating Technique while killing a Primordial will turn it into a Neverborn.<br /> <br /> I don't follow the logic of turning it an Air Breathing Mermaid situation where the Solars needed 4 or 5 other Charms to perma-kill a Primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also say Merela slew a primordial by herself with her bare hands. Technically true, but not accurate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T00:12:40-08:00","id":417308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=417298#post417298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also say Merela slew a primordial by herself with her bare hands. Technically true, but not accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't. That's just what the echo chamber says.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lands of Creation page 13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She'd once been Creation's preeminent warrior and general, and had slain a Primordial with her bare hands, but pursuit of peaceful projects during the time since the war's conclusion had allowed those Solars at the Ochre Fountain's periphery to make their talents to equal hers.</div> </div> </div> </div>She killed a Primordial with her bare hands, hardly unreasonable, and there's nothing about her doing it all by herself. Martial Artists and brawlers often use their bare hands instead of other weapons (indeed, via Charms their bare hands can be equal to weapons), so this line was more a comment on what her combat style is (bare-handed brawler).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T00:37:51-08:00","id":417316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=417308#post417308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it doesn't. That's just what the echo chamber says.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> She killed a Primordial with her bare hands, hardly unreasonable, and there's nothing about her doing it all by herself. Martial Artists and brawlers often use their bare hands instead of other weapons (indeed, via Charms their bare hands can be equal to weapons), so this line was more a comment on what her combat style is (bare-handed brawler).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok then let me put it like this. People don't treat it as &quot;After much grueling battle and work was done to destroy the Primordial. The Ghost-Eating Technique was employed in the death blow to scatter the foes essence and prevent it from reforming.&quot; They treat it as &quot;I can stab a spot in the ground repeatedly and because I used Ghost-Eating Technique that stabbing of the ground destroyed the Endless Desert.&quot; It is not fun, it makes everything about the Yozi and Primodials superfluous, and its so damn anti-climactic as to be asinine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T00:39:52-08:00","id":417318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=417279#post417279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't understand. The rules for Ghost Eating Technique are pretty clear (remove a spirit's last health level while using the Charm and it activates). And the charm says it was used to slay the Neverborn. So it seems clear that using Ghost Eating Technique while killing a Primordial will turn it into a Neverborn.<br /> <br /> I don't follow the logic of turning it an Air Breathing Mermaid situation where the Solars needed 4 or 5 other Charms to perma-kill a Primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because removing a primordial's last health level is not something you can do just by hitting it a few times with a sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T01:05:43-08:00","id":417332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=417316#post417316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok then let me put it like this. People don't treat it as &quot;After much grueling battle and work was done to destroy the Primordial. The Ghost-Eating Technique was employed in the death blow to scatter the foes essence and prevent it from reforming.&quot; They treat it as &quot;I can stab a spot in the ground repeatedly and because I used Ghost-Eating Technique that stabbing of the ground destroyed the Endless Desert.&quot; It is not fun, it makes everything about the Yozi and Primodials superfluous, and its so damn anti-climactic as to be asinine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who are these people? They sound like tools and I'm glad I don't game with them!<br /> <br /> That said, I think it's pretty clear-cut in 2nd edition. If you stab a Yozi's Jouten so many times it dies, and you use ghost eating technique when it happens, then it turns into a Neverborn. Of course, stabbing a Primordial death isn't exactly easy, considering how much soak and how many health levels many of their Jouten would have. Trying to stab the prison-world of Malfeas to death would be rather like trying to stab Creation to death. I mean, I guess in theory you could, but it would probably take you a long, long, long time.<br /> <br /> If you want to stab Cecelyne into a Neverborn you're probably going to want to find a Jouten that isn't an endless, infinite desert with, presumably, nigh-infinite health levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T03:59:16-08:00","id":417415,"title":"","content":"I would rule that every grain of sand in Cecelyne represents one health level. Now, if anyone is capable of stabbing an infinite number of grains of sand, it's a solar, so I feel they still have a fair shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T06:03:27-08:00","id":417465,"title":"","content":"I'll point out that in my example, the goal is <b>not</b> to kill Malfeas.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">I was merely using the targeting of a charm (which AoEs around the victim) with the <b>one</b> target who happens to be within range of <b>everyone</b> (by defining the entire realm). And this would have been irrelevant in the Primordial War, because Malfeas was not a prison.<br /> <br /> Essentially, less &quot;my Solar can single-handedly slaughter all of Malfeas&quot; and more &quot;my Solar can be a massive dick and brutalize innocent demon species, while the Primordials just get annoyed&quot;.</span><br /> <br /> Also, Insignificant Embers Intuition says it &quot;discerns the strength and aspect of the target's Essence relative to his ow it is &quot;not a means of bypassing stealth&quot; and &quot;costs no motes&quot; (for Essence 4+) but &quot;still requires a Charm activation&quot;. And it's vastly inferior to it's predecessor, Theion's Burning Gaze of the Firmament, which adds (Essence) successes to the perception roll, which lets him focus his gaze into wrath (creating an instant Intimacy of righteous anger or hatred), and which <b>then</b> compliments many other Theion charms to punish those Intimacies.<br /> <br /> So it's much easier to curbstomp Malfeas - avoid being seen - even as his subjects burn in holy fire. Malfeas can probably just soak or take the aggravated damage without flinching - the idea is to torment the others.<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> And even if this gets broken, well, again - the goal <b>wasn't</b> to play a &quot;Holy Solar killing demons&quot;.<br /> <br /> The example was &quot;a complete asshole demonologist Solar&quot; who &quot;abuses Holy keywords to reign over demonkind&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hence my Infernals are often Batman (heroes born from tragedy) and my Solars are Superman in Injustice (a horrid god-king).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T06:33:24-08:00","id":417478,"title":"","content":"You can't stab someone in the face and hide from them at the same time. That would be ridiculous. As soon as Malf feels the attack he's going to drop a street on the offending area. He doesn't <i>need</i> to actually detect you personally. It would be like swatting a mosquito.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T06:40:11-08:00","id":417481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=417478#post417478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't stab someone in the face and hide from them at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course you can, that's what invisibility is for. Also Sidereals.<br /> *Avoidance-Katas away, leaving only the Natural Mental Influence of the post behind*<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T06:52:49-08:00","id":417488,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure &quot;within Essence x 3 yards&quot; refers to the user and not the target anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T07:09:41-08:00","id":417502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=417488#post417488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly sure &quot;within Essence x 3 yards&quot; refers to the user and not the target anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>You break my heart - the rules never specified, but yeah, that's a valid interpretation too if you want to be boring. I never wanted to <i>officially</i> default to that because there are so many awesome &quot;inbetween scale&quot; options - for example, if a bunch of Creatures of Darkness are riding a demonic war-elephant, it seems logically that making the elephant erupt in holy fire would harm the other CoDs on it's back (as opposed to, say, &quot;you kicked the elephant's ankle, so the riders are completely safe, even as their mount dissolves to fire&quot;).<br /> <br /> So now you're saying I must <b>become</b> Malfeas and then cock-punch myself. Gotcha.<br /> <br /> Or maybe create a Celestial-tier charm (this is a Terrestrial Martial Art charm I'm referring to) in order to &quot;upgrade&quot; the range.<br /> <br /> I imagine a Solar with Primordial Principle Emulation (from the SMA) could turn itself into a weather system and rain glowing golden holy rain that happens to burn CoDs like acid. <br /> <br /> Derp.<br /> <br /> Conversely, and for the most part, I just <b>really</b> like the idea of an Exalt doing our own version of<b> Hercules vs Augean Stables</b> (where he redirected an entire river, with a boulder, to clean out stables that once held over 1,000 cattle and had not be cleaned in over 30 years). It'd be like a <b>Kung Fu Feng Shui</b>, where the Solar is a scalpel cutting into a Yozi or Neverborn world-body, trying to realign the essence and build something new.<br /> <br /> Even if it is as chaotically stupid as &quot;Oh, Oramus is trapped within his own wings&quot; - &quot;ok, I'll cut through the fucking wings to let him out - then maybe stitch the wings together again once they're unfurled&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T07:44:03-08:00","id":417530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=417465#post417465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I &quot;my Solar can be a massive dick and brutalize innocent demon species, while the Primordials just get annoyed&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And honestly, if your Solar <b>isn't</b> a massive dick, you've diverted from the inspirational materials, and should be ashamed for &quot;doing it wrong&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5154-cappadocius","name":"cappadocius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T08:02:47-08:00","id":417538,"title":"","content":"I assume that at the very least, you can't kill a Primordial until after you kill and ghost-eat all its souls.<br /> <br /> I think Solars should be able to be decent folks, at least according to their own societies. The idea that the Great Curse requires us to play nothing but inhuman monsters spoils a lot of the fun of making my own character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T08:15:29-08:00","id":417545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=417538#post417538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that at the very least, you can't kill a Primordial until after you kill and ghost-eat all its souls.<br /> <br /> I think Solars should be able to be decent folks, at least according to their own societies. The idea that the Great Curse requires us to play nothing but inhuman monsters spoils a lot of the fun of making my own character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the other post is a bit sarcastic. Solars shouldn't be required to be Lawful Good, nor should they required to be totally in line with their mythic inspirations (who were all pretty dickish). I've seen Solars played between those extremes pretty frequently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=417308#post417308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She killed a Primordial with her bare hands, hardly unreasonable, and there's nothing about her doing it all by herself. Martial Artists and brawlers often use their bare hands instead of other weapons (indeed, via Charms their bare hands can be equal to weapons), so this line was more a comment on what her combat style is (bare-handed brawler).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah people interpreted that as &quot;soloed the Primordial&quot; for stupid reasons. In all likelihood multiple Celestials and a score of DBs were fighting it, and she happened to be the one in the best position to put it down for good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T08:32:32-08:00","id":417571,"title":"","content":"My take has always been that Primordials are simultaneously physical and spiritual - just like Autochtonia (which is how they explain that you can't just dematerialize and walk through walls in Autochtonia). <br /> <br /> As 3rd Circle Souls, Deva must also be simultaneously physical and spiritual - Ligier is a Demon and a Green Sun (and the source of all light); Munaxes is a Demon and a Ravine (and a bottomless pit); Amalion is a Demon and a Manse (and the forebearer of many and all her manses); Ipithymia, the Street of Gold Lanterns, etc, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> <b>Thus</b> the idea of geomantically combating or &quot;pruning&quot; the Yozis is much like what we saw in Autochtonia - sure, you can kill Autochton's primary souls <b>but</b> the First and Forsaken Lion <b>also achieves victory</b> by sabotaging and wrecking and misaligning the world-body. <b>In this view, Debok Moom</b> is simultaneously Autochton's belligerent inspiration - his immune system - the temple-factory-complex that produces war-machines - and in itself, the same factory-complex is whatever organ is regulating his immune response. <b>Likewise</b>, Malfeas isn't a lifeless crust - if I bring destruction to the Street of Gold Lanterns, to the Manses of Amalion, if I shoot the Green Sun out of the sky with my bow - then I'm <b>also</b> waging violence against demons <b>and</b> Malfeas.<br /> <br /> There's no artificial distinction between all these things.<br /> <br /> They're not gods - who merely <i>shepherd </i>the cities and domains they watch. They <b>are</b> the domains.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that at the very least, you can't kill a Primordial until after you kill and ghost-eat all its souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this.<br /> <br /> But one problem I have with the setting..... is that if you kill the Fetich, everyone else allegedly just vanishes. Oh, Malfeas has 23+ top tier demons that are awesome? Murder Ligier and the others implode.<br /> <br /> Which can be fun (for sheer ripple-effect destruction) but makes me wonder whether we can have any sense of continuity --- what if some of those other demons were kind of awesome, how can I best help them &quot;splinter off&quot; (Lunar or Sidereal charms?). Wyld exposure? What if we wanted to kill Ligier - but give the &quot;crown&quot; to another demon. Shouldn't a yet-living 3rd Circle serve as a better &quot;inheritor&quot; and &quot;seed&quot; than a completely splattered Fetich? This may be some Scion inspiration (where it sounds like the Primordial is <b>Terra</b>, it's Fetich is <b>Gaia, </b>and other 3rd-Circle &quot;Avatars&quot; variously ally or want to usurp her position). Stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that &quot;as written&quot;, it doesn't seem like you need to kill them all. Just kill the Fetich with ghost-eating technique. The remaining demons probably either get dragged to death with the Primordial <b>or</b> splinter off as new behemoths and hecatonshire.<br /> <br /> And &quot;as written&quot;, an equally possible interpretation is that you kill the Fetich - the Primordial needs to reform - <i>and all the other demons die too</i>, to be recycled and reshaped. Killing them &quot;in the womb&quot; is a lot easier via this interpretation too.<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> And then, if 3rd Circles could replace the Fetich - what if you kill the Fetich and 2 or 3 of the 3rd Circles can't agree on the new leadership? Could they splinter off and form 2 or 3 smaller Primordials? Will they automatically be weaker than the original? What if they begin recruiting more souls to flesh out their ranks?<br /> <br /> Etc, etc, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T09:49:45-08:00","id":417618,"title":"","content":"If the Primordial reforms then they generate new 3rd Circle souls and a new Fetich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T10:00:06-08:00","id":417625,"title":"","content":"I imagine a few of the &quot;new&quot; third circle souls could potentially be more or less unchanged from the previous incarnation, and still have their memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T14:09:26-08:00","id":422208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=410315#post410315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I checked a dictionary. It does mean what I think it means.<br /> <br /> What people are objecting to is how the Redemption narrative for Abyssals relate to the theme of Solars, this being: &quot;the consequences of the use of power&quot;, and how it just assumes that any an all uses of Solar power are morally superior to Abyssal power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Going by this argument your comment makes even less sense. If splat theme makes little difference for individual Exalts and they are guided by their own in character moral compass... Why would they want to become part of the Evil Solar Anathema? And what does it matter how good or evil individual Solars are presented in the books? It isn't like any random Abyssal has access to their writeups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, since you understand what a theme is, why are you complaining? The movement of darkness to light and back again is &quot;in theme&quot; for Solars. If it wasn't, the Abyssals would not exist as they are. As a point of fact, the original Exaltation of Solars uplifts them to a state of light, and their fall at the Usurpation and sealing away, which consigned them to death forever, was a movement to darkness. Their return then, is a return to light--or darkness, as witnessed in the game's sell-line: will they save the world or destroy it? Indeed, a real live Solar can become an Abyssal, again another signifier of light to darkness. And indeed, an Abyssal can become a Solar, a movement from darkness to light.<br /> <br /> Anyone can point out a pattern, a motif, or a theme in the colloquial sense. People who understand literary themes can tell you how they work, and they can see that the above has been established as a theme of the Solar and Abyssal Exalted resoundingly, over and over, since day one.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T15:35:38-08:00","id":422250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=417538#post417538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that at the very least, you can't kill a Primordial until after you kill and ghost-eat all its souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way this is phrased makes it sound like murdering one of the transcendent horrors that created the world would play out like <i>Kill Bill</i>. <br /> <br /> I suspect part of the problem is that it\u2019s a mechanical answer to a narrative question. When we say, \u201cThe Exalted were the only ones who could kill the Primordials because they have the ghost-eating charms\u201d what we mean is \u201cFrodo was the only one who could carry the One Ring all the way to Mount Doom.\u201d<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:32:07-08:00","id":422299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422208#post422208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, since you understand what a theme is, why are you complaining? The movement of darkness to light and back again is &quot;in theme&quot; for Solars. If it wasn't, the Abyssals would not exist as they are. As a point of fact, the original Exaltation of Solars uplifts them to a state of light, and their fall at the Usurpation and sealing away, which consigned them to death forever, was a movement to darkness. Their return then, is a return to light--or darkness, as witnessed in the game's sell-line: will they save the world or destroy it? Indeed, a real live Solar can become an Abyssal, again another signifier of light to darkness. And indeed, an Abyssal can become a Solar, a movement from darkness to light.<br /> <br /> Anyone can point out a pattern, a motif, or a theme in the colloquial sense. People who understand literary themes can tell you how they work, and they can see that the above has been established as a theme of the Solar and Abyssal Exalted resoundingly, over and over, since day one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is all in line with the cycle of night and day, yes I'm aware. It doesn't take a genius to notice, after all it's written all over the Caste names of both Solars and Abyssals.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless I think you misunderstand my objection (I would't really call it a complain and it certainly isn't directed at the concept of Redemption itself) to how you dismissed the concerns of all the people who posted in this thread by stating that the problem was that the Solar NPCs were badly written.<br /> <br /> There is more to it than that.<br /> <br /> People are concerned over how Redemption seems to imply that the Solar Exalted are inherently moral and I personally think that the point made about why anyone would want to become one when everything they know paints them as the worst monsters to ever exists has some merit and deserves more than that. There is also the questions about how Redemption undermines the larger theme of Exalted of &quot;actions have consequences&quot; by undoing one of the worst consequences that the Exalted Host and the order imposed by Heaven has suffered as a whole.<br /> <br /> As far as I know none of this changes no matter how well written your Solars NPCs are.<br /> <br /> Also, by the tone of your reply I realize I wasn't being clear in my previous post: I'm not a native English speaker, so when someone that actually is one tells me I don't know what a word means I check. I literally went and checked the word &quot;theme&quot; in a dictionary just to be sure it wasn't a false friend. I wasn't being facetious or anything like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","user":"Ravraxas","date":". 02-27-2015, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:37:40-08:00","id":422302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422299#post422299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is all in line with the cycle of night and day, yes I'm aware. It doesn't take a genius to notice, after all it's written all over the Caste names of both Solars and Abyssals.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless I think you misunderstand my objection (I would't really call it a complain and it certainly isn't directed at the concept of Redemption itself) to how you dismissed the concerns of all the people who posted in this thread by stating that the problem was that the Solar NPCs were badly written.<br /> <br /> There is more to it than that.<br /> <br /> People are concerned over how Redemption seems to imply that the Solar Exalted are inherently moral and, personally, I think that the point made about why anyone would want to become one when everything they know paints them as the worst monsters to ever exists has some merit and deserves more than that. There also the questions about how Redemption undermines the larger theme of Exalted of &quot;actions have consequences&quot; by undoing one of the worst consequences that the Exalted Host and the order imposed by Heaven has suffered as a whole.<br /> <br /> As far as I know none of this changes no matter how well written you'r Solars NPCs are.<br /> <br /> Also, by the tone of you'r reply I realize I wasn't being clear in my previous post: I'm not a native English speaker, so when someone that actually is one tells me I don't know what a word means I check. I literally went and checked the word &quot;theme&quot; in a dictionary just to be sure it wasn't a false friend. I wasn't being facetious or anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally what I have taken over the years from the idea of Abyssal redemption is that while being a Solar is not in and of itself a state of being that gives certainty of moral superiority. But that the nature of the Abyssal exaltation is more conducive to Creation ending badly in some sort of meaningful sense. It's an extremely fine line to make because if you push that too far and too incoherently then Abyssal fans feel like they're being told that they are terrible people for liking Abyssals. Make it meaningless and the Deathlord motivations for making Abyssals thing W vs thing X,Y, or Z become nonsensical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T17:53:22-08:00","id":422368,"title":"","content":"Abyssal exaltation is inherently destructive. Its power is derived from beings whose only desire is the death of everything.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that Solar exaltation is inherently good, but it is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T18:00:11-08:00","id":422370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422299#post422299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is all in line with the cycle of night and day, yes I'm aware. It doesn't take a genius to notice, after all it's written all over the Caste names of both Solars and Abyssals.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless I think you misunderstand my objection (I would't really call it a complain and it certainly isn't directed at the concept of Redemption itself) to how you dismissed the concerns of all the people who posted in this thread by stating that the problem was that the Solar NPCs were badly written.<br /> <br /> There is more to it than that.<br /> <br /> People are concerned over how Redemption seems to imply that the Solar Exalted are inherently moral and I personally think that the point made about why anyone would want to become one when everything they know paints them as the worst monsters to ever exists has some merit and deserves more than that. There is also the questions about how Redemption undermines the larger theme of Exalted of &quot;actions have consequences&quot; by undoing one of the worst consequences that the Exalted Host and the order imposed by Heaven has suffered as a whole.<br /> <br /> As far as I know none of this changes no matter how well written your Solars NPCs are.<br /> <br /> Also, by the tone of your reply I realize I wasn't being clear in my previous post: I'm not a native English speaker, so when someone that actually is one tells me I don't know what a word means I check. I literally went and checked the word &quot;theme&quot; in a dictionary just to be sure it wasn't a false friend. I wasn't being facetious or anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Golconda in Vampire: the Masquerade was implied, at first, to allow you to become human again - or to, at least, save your soul like a human's is saved.<br /> <br /> It involved becoming an ascetic saint.<br /> <br /> Does that make a statement that humanity is inherently moral? Or just that to cast a curse to your very nature away one must be as a saint?<br /> <br /> You are drawing the wrong inference from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T19:09:12-08:00","id":422454,"title":"","content":"Redemption (as is being discussed here) as <i><b>exactly nothing</b></i> to do with morals. Or morality. In any way. Wanting it or not wanting is not dictate whether your character is behaving morally or not. That's up to your character to decide. That's kinda how morals work.<br /> <br /> EDIT: or rather does not indicate that one is morally superior to the other. at is up to the character/player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 02-27-2015, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T19:15:49-08:00","id":422460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422299#post422299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is all in line with the cycle of night and day, yes I'm aware. It doesn't take a genius to notice, after all it's written all over the Caste names of both Solars and Abyssals.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless I think you misunderstand my objection (I would't really call it a complain and it certainly isn't directed at the concept of Redemption itself) to how you dismissed the concerns of all the people who posted in this thread by stating that the problem was that the Solar NPCs were badly written.<br /> <br /> There is more to it than that.<br /> <br /> People are concerned over how Redemption seems to imply that the Solar Exalted are inherently moral and I personally think that the point made about why anyone would want to become one when everything they know paints them as the worst monsters to ever exists has some merit and deserves more than that. There is also the questions about how Redemption undermines the larger theme of Exalted of &quot;actions have consequences&quot; by undoing one of the worst consequences that the Exalted Host and the order imposed by Heaven has suffered as a whole.<br /> <br /> As far as I know none of this changes no matter how well written your Solars NPCs are.<br /> <br /> Also, by the tone of your reply I realize I wasn't being clear in my previous post: I'm not a native English speaker, so when someone that actually is one tells me I don't know what a word means I check. I literally went and checked the word &quot;theme&quot; in a dictionary just to be sure it wasn't a false friend. I wasn't being facetious or anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First let me just say that, I am only offering you these remarks because I am trying to take your criticism to heart\u2014but it's difficult if I don't understand your meaning. Now that you have made yourself very clear, let's start again, shall we?<br /> <br /> There's nothing in a Solar's powers that makes everything they do turn out &quot;Good&quot; or moral. But the Abyssal curse guarantees everything they do will end in ash and sorrow. To an Abyssal suffering this curse, the motive/creative/holy power of Solar Exaltation represents not a guarantee of a state of moral good, but the <i>chance</i> to do moral good as he deems it, without bringing ruin and death to everyone and everything he loves as a guaranteed promise of his power. An Abyssal who wants to break the curse would rise to the lofty heights of sainthood in pursuing this goal, despite the awful price in suffering he must pay. It has everything to do with the Abyssal's idea of morality and how the Unconquered Sun recognizes a hero's virtue, and that Solars have the choice of good or evil. Redemption does not mean the Abyssal who has become a Solar will be free from temptation and unable to make mistakes or act immorally, although it is highly implied that they will stay a moral actor by virtue of what they have suffered.<br /> <br /> And yes, this all requires the ST to deem actions moral, which some may reject outright. Those kinds of Storytellers won't run Redemption stories, and that's AOK, but other Storytellers doing so won't hurt their games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":86,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","user":"John M\u00f8rke","date":". 02-27-2015, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T19:39:58-08:00","id":422490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422460#post422460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has everything to do with the Abyssal's idea of morality and how the Unconquered Sun recognizes a hero's virtue,</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of interjecting myself, I'd like to note that a lot of people seem to have a real problem with the Unconquered Sun being held up as an exemplar of virtue of morality and qualified to render judgments of that sort. I forget if it was in this thread or another, but there was a guy recently grousing about how in his games, the only message the UCS had for the Solars was &quot;go away and do your jobs so I can keep doing crack.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T21:19:39-08:00","id":422589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422490#post422490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the risk of interjecting myself, I'd like to note that a lot of people seem to have a real problem with the Unconquered Sun being held up as an exemplar of virtue of morality and qualified to render judgments of that sort. I forget if it was in this thread or another, but there was a guy recently grousing about how in his games, the only message the UCS had for the Solars was &quot;go away and do your jobs so I can keep doing crack.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are welcome to that depiction, but the Unconquered Sun literally evaluates an Abyssal seeking Redemption, so I think it's safe to say that such an ST is employing an ST's prerogative. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T21:34:49-08:00","id":422597,"title":"","content":"If we get anything out of Ex3, I would love it to be a fanbase that doesn't consider &quot;engaging with the game as written&quot; to be acting as a kindergartener.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3806-dwho","name":"dwho","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T21:35:26-08:00","id":422598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422490#post422490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd like to note that a lot of people seem to have a real problem with the Unconquered Sun being held up as an exemplar of virtue of morality and qualified to render judgments of that sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth pointing out that the first half of this sentence doesn't necessarily go with the second half. <br /> <br /> It's entirely valid to question whether the concept of heroism as seen by the Unconquered Sun is an ideal worth living up to, but there is literally no-one more qualified to decide who becomes a Solar than the Sun. Anyone who becomes a golden light has to accept his judgement in some form or other. <br /> <br /> If a character doesn't think the has anything to offer then why are they trying to get into his club? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T22:32:29-08:00","id":422624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422598#post422598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's worth pointing out that the first half of this sentence doesn't necessarily go with the second half.<br /> <br /> It's entirely valid to question whether the concept of heroism as seen by the Unconquered Sun is an ideal worth living up to, but there is literally no-one more qualified to decide who becomes a Solar than the Sun. Anyone who becomes a golden light has to accept his judgement in some form or other.<br /> <br /> If a character doesn't think the has anything to offer then why are they trying to get into his club?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the impression I've always gotten is that it puts people who think the Unconquered Sun is really horrible at his job at best or a noxious, drug-addicted hypocrite at worst into a bit of a bind re: Abyssals. They can either labor under the Abyssal curse and know that just about everything they do is going to redound to the benefit of the Neverborn in some way... or they can pursue the obvious way to get out from under that curse, which is to get the blessing and approval of someone they hold in contempt who is getting high as a kite in the Jade Pleasure Dome in-between blowjobs from Saturn to lift it.<br /> <br /> This isn't a big problem for people such as myself who see Sol as genuinely, for-reals heroic and virtuous and an actual exemplar of things that are good and right (which is how I think he's intended to be viewed by the line devs as a whole) but a lot of people <i>don't</i> see him that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T23:14:22-08:00","id":422637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422624#post422624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the impression I've always gotten is that it puts people who think the Unconquered Sun is really horrible at his job at best or a noxious, drug-addicted hypocrite at worst into a bit of a bind re: Abyssals. They can either labor under the Abyssal curse and know that just about everything they do is going to redound to the benefit of the Neverborn in some way... or they can pursue the obvious way to get out from under that curse, which is to get the blessing and approval of someone they hold in contempt who is getting high as a kite in the Jade Pleasure Dome in-between blowjobs from Saturn to lift it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me this is a profound Character Concept Fail. <br /> <br /> It's fine to play any character as rejecting their patron and making their own way. A Solar may very well throw up the grand middle finger to the Unconquered Sun and never follow the visions he's given, no matter how insistent they become. An Abyssal might renouce his leige and resolve to do the best he can, shouldering the burden of the dark fate. That's all fine. But an Abyssal seeking redemption is explicitly requesting the mandate of the Unconquered Sun. It's rediculous to suggest that this character should expect to say 'I hold you and everything you are in contempt, but please empower me!'. <br /> <br /> My question, looking at this would not be 'Why is the Sun the way he is?', but 'why does this player, rejecting basically every long term option for an Abyssal, want to play and Abyssal in the first place?'. Unless the story is that good intentions are always blunted, even after death (which might be made into a good story, for those so inclined!) it seems like it's best for everyone that these players were just not playing Abyssals in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T01:56:06-08:00","id":422718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422460#post422460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Abyssal curse guarantees everything they do will end in ash and sorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>This... sounds an aweful lot like &quot;the only way to play a heroc Abyssal is to seek redemption, because as long as you're an Abyssal, everything will get worse&quot;.<br /> Or can an Abyssal at least focus said &quot;ash and sorrow&quot; on their enemies, if they're satisfied with bringing doom to those they think deserve it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T02:21:13-08:00","id":422731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422718#post422718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the only way to play a heroc Abyssal is to seek redemption</div> </div> </div> </div>The only way to play an heroic Abyssal is to try. Whether that's trying for redemption or just trying to do enough good to offset the harm you cause by existing. You may succeed, you may fail. That's the point. <br /> <br /> More explicitly, in an Heroic Abyssal narative the question is 'Am I ultimately a force for good?'. Only the genuinely heroic answer should be 'yes'. That means on balance all Abyssals will be fundamentally corrosive, whether they like it or not. Overcoming that requires a continual, concerted effort, and shouldn't be a magical power that you can only nleash on the deserving when you feel like it. <br /> <br /> Abysalls have a heroisim of struggle, and internal conflict and never getting the ticker-tape-parade. If you're not on borad with that you shoulfd ask why your character is Abyssal in the firstplace. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T04:50:40-08:00","id":422814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422718#post422718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This... sounds an aweful lot like &amp;quot;the only way to play a heroc Abyssal is to seek redemption, because as long as you're an Abyssal, everything will get worse&amp;quot;.<br /> Or can an Abyssal at least focus said &amp;quot;ash and sorrow&amp;quot; on their enemies, if they're satisfied with bringing doom to those they think deserve it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, Abyssals are designed by the neverborn such that no matter what they do, they're lessening Creation.<br /> <br /> Destroyed the soul of that one warlord that was threatening genocide? Good. One less soul in the cycle of reincarnation.<br /> Using ghosts to empower necromancy? Good. See above.<br /> Trying to hang out with living friends? Good. You're building resonance.<br /> Throwing crypt bolts? Good. Necrotize ALL the things!<br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> No matter what they do, the neverborn are rubbing their hands and muttering &quot;goood... Goood... Eeexcellent&quot;... When they're not howling in endless agony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T07:06:25-08:00","id":422876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422718#post422718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This... sounds an aweful lot like &quot;the only way to play a heroc Abyssal is to seek redemption, because as long as you're an Abyssal, everything will get worse&quot;.<br /> Or can an Abyssal at least focus said &quot;ash and sorrow&quot; on their enemies, if they're satisfied with bringing doom to those they think deserve it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to argue that Abyssals weren't problematic in certain ways. Remember, I am discussing what was in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T08:10:15-08:00","id":422944,"title":"","content":"I don't dislike redemption but I think Second Edition gave it an unfortunate urgency via mirror charms, the Resonance rules and the prospect of being a Solar cured of the Great Curse. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T09:38:44-08:00","id":423049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422460#post422460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To an Abyssal suffering this curse, the motive/creative/holy power of Solar Exaltation represents not a guarantee of a state of moral good, but the <i>chance</i> to do moral good as he deems it, <b>without bringing ruin and death to everyone and everything he loves as a guaranteed promise of his power. </b></div> </div> </div> </div>&amp; from a different post...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422876#post422876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to argue that Abyssals weren't problematic in certain ways. Remember, I am discussing what was in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to belabor the point, but I'm not clear on if the first above statement is a baked in part of being an Abyssal in Third Edition, or is that part of the 2nd Edition lore that might not necessarily make its way into Third Edition.<br /> <br /> Really, I just want to play an Abyssal without also feeling like I'm giving my ST a free pass screw up all my characters long term goals as often as they'd like in the name of a doomed narrative.<br /> <br /> To spin it another way, Can my Abyssals power be recognized as merely <i>strange</i> or <i>uncanny </i>to the land of the living, or is it always going to be maleficent in a &quot;kill it its evil&quot; kinda way?<br /> <br /> For instance, I've been going through the Elric saga, and there's some interesting ideas about power and evil &amp; etc in there . . . Can an abyssal who is not out to destroy Creation use his or her power without feeling like they're Elric drawing Strombringer once again, calling on something that is an ontological evil, whose use carries a price that existence will one day be forced to pay?<br /> Is the only way out of that cycle to be redeemed back into a Solar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T09:44:00-08:00","id":423058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423049#post423049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp; from a different post...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sorry to belabor the point, but I'm not clear on if the first above statement is a baked in part of being an Abyssal in Third Edition, or is that part of the 2nd Edition lore that might not necessarily make its way into Third Edition.<br /> <br /> Really, I just want to play an Abyssal without also feeling like I'm giving my ST a free pass screw up all my characters long term goals as often as they'd like in the name of a doomed narrative.<br /> <br /> To spin it another way, Can my Abyssals power be recognized as merely <i>strange</i> or <i>uncanny </i>to the land of the living, or is it always going to be maleficent in a &quot;kill it its evil&quot; kinda way?<br /> <br /> For instance, I've been going through the Elric saga, and there's some interesting ideas about power and evil &amp; etc in there . . . Can an abyssal who is not out to destroy Creation use his or her power without feeling like they're Elric drawing Strombringer once again, calling on something that is an ontological evil, whose use carries a price that existence will one day be forced to pay?<br /> Is the only way out of that cycle to be redeemed back into a Solar?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am explicitly discussing the way Abyssals were in previous editions, as a means of explaining the meaning of Redemption. I think if I respond to your questions about EX3 here, it will make my earlier posts an unintentional endorsement of certain things we might not endorse in future books. If you would like to ask some questions about Abyssals in EX3 in a separate thread, I will try to answer them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T09:47:25-08:00","id":423062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423058#post423058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am explicitly discussing the way Abyssals were in previous editions, as a means of explaining the meaning of Redemption. I think if I respond to your questions about EX3 here, it will make my earlier posts an unintentional endorsement of certain things we might not endorse in future books. If you would like to ask some questions about Abyssals in EX3 in a separate thread, I will try to answer them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally understandable and I understand the necessity of not nailing anything down, especially while there is not necessarily anything to lay down. I appreciate the clarification =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T11:40:55-08:00","id":423149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422637#post422637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question, looking at this would not be 'Why is the Sun the way he is?', but 'why does this player, rejecting basically every long term option for an Abyssal, want to play and Abyssal in the first place?'. Unless the story is that good intentions are always blunted, even after death (which might be made into a good story, for those so inclined!) it seems like it's best for everyone that these players were just not playing Abyssals in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, hmm.<br /> <br /> From my perspective, and this is me trying to do tea-leaf reading so it may be wrong, there are a lot of people who...<br /> <br /> 1) Would like to play an Abyssal, but...<br /> <br /> 2) Don't want them to turn into a Solar, for a variety of reasons including but not limited to rejecting the moral authority of the Unconqured Sun to declare that they're not evil and are in fact heroes,<br /> <br /> 3) Don't want to pursue the annihilation of Creation, and<br /> <br /> 4) Don't want to labor under the Abyssal Curse of everything they touch redounding to the ultimate benefit of the Neverborn.<br /> <br /> This has always kind of baffled me. The whole point of playing an Abyssal, it has always seemed to me, is that you agreed to the agenda of Oblivion, for whatever reason, and now you have to decide between either serving that agenda with your whole heart, or rejecting it and starting the long slow climb towards redemption and returning the Black Exaltation you bear to its true state, free of the taint of the Neverborn. There's always been a potential third path, where you decide to usurp the Deathlords and then just not pursue Oblivion, but the Underworld by its very nature serves Oblivion, so... yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only way to play an heroic Abyssal is to try. Whether that's trying for redemption or just trying to do enough good to offset the harm you cause by existing. You may succeed, you may fail. That's the point.<br /> <br /> More explicitly, in an Heroic Abyssal narative the question is 'Am I ultimately a force for good?'. Only the genuinely heroic answer should be 'yes'. That means on balance all Abyssals will be fundamentally corrosive, whether they like it or not. Overcoming that requires a continual, concerted effort, and shouldn't be a magical power that you can only nleash on the deserving when you feel like it.<br /> <br /> Abysalls have a heroisim of struggle, and internal conflict and never getting the ticker-tape-parade. If you're not on borad with that you shoulfd ask why your character is Abyssal in the firstplace. </div> </div> </div>Exactly!<br /> <br /> And the thing is those are very interesting narratives, and the splat is very, very up-front about those being your options! The implementation has often kind of sucked but it isn't like anyone is getting bait and switched here. I understand people wanting more options but... I dunno. In my less charitable moments I think &quot;people just want to play a black-glowing thrill-kill Solar with awesome ultimate death powers that have no real downside&quot; but there have been enough thoughtful posts about the issues people have with Abyssals I'm uncomfortable just dismissing them so cavalierly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423049#post423049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, I just want to play an Abyssal without also feeling like I'm giving my ST a free pass screw up all my characters long term goals as often as they'd like in the name of a doomed narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would submit, Janissary, that if this is a genuine fear on your part the problem isn't with Abyssals, it is with your GM. Assuming that your characters long-term goals are also your long-term goals as a player, your GM should be helping you fulfill them, not screwing them up. At the very least they should be upfront that they're never going to happen and you had best pick some new ones. I've had GMs tell me point blank &quot;what your character wants is never going to happen. If that's okay with you and you're playing some doomed martyr, great! I'll help you tell that story. If you actually mean for them to triumph, you should leave the table now, because your goals are incompatible with and toxic towards the goals of literally everyone else in the group and this is a group game.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you're sitting down at a table and worried that your GM is about to dick you over, you should probably get up and walk away right then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To spin it another way, Can my Abyssals power be recognized as merely strange or uncanny to the land of the living, or is it always going to be maleficent in a &quot;kill it its evil&quot; kinda way? </div> </div> </div>You can probably use your cool death powers in a way that people don't immediately respond to as &quot;kill it is evil&quot; but that doesn't mean they won't actually be evil. I think that Holden <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:green-sun-bullseyes\" target=\"_blank\">said it best:</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The average group of Exalts is not going to care. Nobody gives a fuck that you're an Infernal, or an Abyssal. .... They will be like 'hey, your powers are weird.' And then will form an opinion based on <i>what you are doing</i> and how you treat them. Later on they may develop misgivings as it becomes apparent that your powers are from <i>Hell</i>, but that is more of a function of you being a creepazoid who makes 'vroom' noises in her sleep and turns people inside-out than an Infernal. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T14:19:18-08:00","id":423436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423149#post423149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, hmm.<br /> <br /> From my perspective, and this is me trying to do tea-leaf reading so it may be wrong, there are a lot of people who...<br /> <br /> 1) Would like to play an Abyssal, but...<br /> <br /> 2) Don't want them to turn into a Solar, for a variety of reasons including but not limited to rejecting the moral authority of the Unconqured Sun to declare that they're not evil and are in fact heroes,<br /> <br /> 3) Don't want to pursue the annihilation of Creation, and<br /> <br /> 4) Don't want to labor under the Abyssal Curse of everything they touch redounding to the ultimate benefit of the Neverborn.<br /> <br /> This has always kind of baffled me. The whole point of playing an Abyssal, it has always seemed to me, is that you agreed to the agenda of Oblivion, for whatever reason, and now you have to decide between either serving that agenda with your whole heart, or rejecting it and starting the long slow climb towards redemption and returning the Black Exaltation you bear to its true state, free of the taint of the Neverborn. There's always been a potential third path, where you decide to usurp the Deathlords and then just not pursue Oblivion, but the Underworld by its very nature serves Oblivion, so... yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the &quot;serves oblivion&quot; part that I'm not down with. I'm in it to tell stories, and Oblivion seems to me (personal taste) rather more like the death of stories in a non-interesting way. To me it inspires exactly one kind of story, Maiden of the Mirthless Smile or Lady of Darkness etc etc, where the thing that makes characters different is, to borrow a page out of the Lunar book, what weapons they wield.<br /> <br /> My argument is based on the idea that the Underworld isn't a cancer eating away at the heart of Creation. That the Ancestor Cult can be interesting and even in some cases beneficial to the living, that, you know, it's bigger than just Skeletor's evil mirror universe. <br /> <br /> I can see why you'd want to portray it that way, but I think think that just leads to an uninteresting Underworld. I want there to be something that's conceivably worth saving in the Underworld, I think it would be cool to see the abyssal go from tool of destruction to something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423149#post423149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the thing is those are very interesting narratives, and the splat is very, very up-front about those being your options! The implementation has often kind of sucked but it isn't like anyone is getting bait and switched here. I understand people wanting more options but... I dunno. In my less charitable moments I think &quot;people just want to play a black-glowing thrill-kill Solar with awesome ultimate death powers that have no real downside&quot; but there have been enough thoughtful posts about the issues people have with Abyssals I'm uncomfortable just dismissing them so cavalierly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking personally (and I suppose reiterating my previous point) I think the Underworld could use a (subjectively compassionate) hero figure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423149#post423149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would submit, Janissary, that if this is a genuine fear on your part the problem isn't with Abyssals, it is with your GM. Assuming that your characters long-term goals are also your long-term goals as a player, your GM should be helping you fulfill them, not screwing them up. At the very least they should be upfront that they're never going to happen and you had best pick some new ones. I've had GMs tell me point blank &quot;what your character wants is never going to happen. If that's okay with you and you're playing some doomed martyr, great! I'll help you tell that story. If you actually mean for them to triumph, you should leave the table now, because your goals are incompatible with and toxic towards the goals of literally everyone else in the group and this is a group game.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you're sitting down at a table and worried that your GM is about to dick you over, you should probably get up and walk away right then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally when I'd run into this problem I'd agree with you, but I've run into instances where an otherwise reasonable, understanding and fun to game with ST disregards reason and class in the pursuit of doing what he or she thinks is expected. But, I mostly play in chat games when I'm not STing, so I admit my view is biased here... <br /> <br /> In any case, I don't expect the writers to tell a ST how to run their games, but that's not the same as hammering away on the doomed fate of Abyssals for pages and pages...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423149#post423149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can probably use your cool death powers in a way that people don't immediately respond to as &quot;kill it is evil&quot; but that doesn't mean they won't actually be evil. I think that Holden <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:green-sun-bullseyes\" target=\"_blank\">said it best:</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm familiar with and absolutely agree with Holden's point. <br /> <br /> My statement wasn't very clear, I'm speaking more to setting statements, which are generally harder to disagree with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T14:48:12-08:00","id":423471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422731#post422731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way to play an heroic Abyssal is to try. Whether that's trying for redemption or just trying to do enough good to offset the harm you cause by existing. You may succeed, you may fail. That's the point.<br /> <br /> More explicitly, in an Heroic Abyssal narative the question is 'Am I ultimately a force for good?'. Only the genuinely heroic answer should be 'yes'. That means on balance all Abyssals will be fundamentally corrosive, whether they like it or not. Overcoming that requires a continual, concerted effort, and shouldn't be a magical power that you can only nleash on the deserving when you feel like it.<br /> <br /> Abysalls have a heroisim of struggle, and internal conflict and never getting the ticker-tape-parade. If you're not on borad with that you shoulfd ask why your character is Abyssal in the firstplace.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I have no problem with this. Being a heroic Abyssal without redemption shouldn't be the easy way, but I think it should be <i>possible</i>. I don't want &quot;Every breath you draw brings the world closer to its complete destruction, unless you change your colour theme&quot;. I would prefer if the doom an Abyssal brings to the world came from them <i>slipping up</i>, with even tiny mistakes - or even simple carelessness - quickly leading to long-term or permanent damage to those around them. [Edit: Or, alternately, if they had to constantly &quot;swim against the stream&quot; - where their existence itself does bring harm in some way, but <i>not</i> irreparable harm to the fabric of creation as a whole, and where their constant effort can actually outweight the destruction they bring... for as long as they keep struggling.] I would prefer them to be <i>dangerous</i>, not <i>inevitably, invariably damaging</i>.<br /> <br /> Basically, what I <i>don't</i> want is this:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422814#post422814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, Abyssals are designed by the neverborn such that no matter what they do, they're lessening Creation.<br /> <br /> Destroyed the soul of that one warlord that was threatening genocide? Good. One less soul in the cycle of reincarnation.<br /> Using ghosts to empower necromancy? Good. See above.<br /> Trying to hang out with living friends? Good. You're building resonance.<br /> Throwing crypt bolts? Good. Necrotize ALL the things!<br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> No matter what they do, the neverborn are rubbing their hands and muttering &quot;goood... Goood... Eeexcellent&quot;... When they're not howling in endless agony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because this? This is just a villain splat. It's D&amp;D's Always Chaotic Evil Drow, including the inevitable &quot;noble drow trying to redeem his evil kin&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423149#post423149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Stuff about not understanding heroic non-redemption Abyssals]</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of the outsider hero. The hero who isn't a part of the world, who never <i>will</i> be a part of the world, yet still chooses to defend it. If all an Abyssal does inevitably brings Creation closer to its doom, then Abyssals can never really protect it unless they redeem themselves. If they can do stuff without diminishing creation, then even if they can never be the shining heroes beloved by all, they can still be a force of good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","user":"Dusk Shine","date":". 02-28-2015, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:00:54-08:00","id":423568,"title":"","content":"Destroying a soul utterly doesn't deprive the cycle of reincarnation of human souls. Humans aren't Dragon Kings and Creation isn't Autochthon. The Well of Souls creates a literally infinite supply of new human baby souls fueled by the infinite Wyld.<br /> <br /> The horror of destroying a soul utterly forever is that you just destroyed somebody's soul. You denied them any possible chance of reincarnation or even an afterlife. Even if they were a horrible genocidal warlord, they'll never have a chance to become a better person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:30:27-08:00","id":423612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423568#post423568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Destroying a soul utterly doesn't deprive the cycle of reincarnation of human souls. Humans aren't Dragon Kings and Creation isn't Autochthon. The Well of Souls creates a literally infinite supply of new human baby souls fueled by the infinite Wyld.<br /> <br /> The horror of destroying a soul utterly forever is that you just destroyed somebody's soul. You denied them any possible chance of reincarnation or even an afterlife. Even if they were a horrible genocidal warlord, they'll never have a chance to become a better person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the idea that an individual retains a recognizable value of self-hood from incarnation to incarnation questionable at best.<br /> <br /> Plenty of religions and philosophies in Creation and the real world believe otherwise, but the setting doesn't specifically give you an answer one way or another.<br /> <br /> Coupling this with the fact that more than a few of the terrible acts in Creation have been justified with &quot;we'll give them a better deal in the next life&quot; seems to me to show that reincarnation isn't the natural and numinous principle it's chalked up to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T05:05:30-08:00","id":423997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423471#post423471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would prefer if the doom an Abyssal brings to the world came from them <i>slipping up</i>, with even tiny mistakes - or even simple carelessness - quickly leading to long-term or permanent damage to those around them. [Edit: Or, alternately, if they had to constantly &quot;swim against the stream&quot; - where their existence itself does bring harm in some way, but <i>not</i> irreparable harm to the fabric of creation as a whole, and where their constant effort can actually outweight the destruction they bring... for as long as they keep struggling.] I would prefer them to be <i>dangerous</i>, not <i>inevitably, invariably damaging</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would actually be harmful to all the Abyssal stories. The heroic one included.<br /> <br /> What it says is 'I can get out of it'. Sure I made this terrible deal to continue living at the expense of the world, but the consequenses of that are entirely under my control. Because I now have good intentions, I avoid all the harm I agreed to represent.<br /> <br /> Going back to speaking more broadly again, every Abyssal story is a tradegdy.Sometimes a heroic tradgedy where ther hero struggles against unwitting consequenses of their own actions. Sometimes a mournful tradgedy where good people are draw down into darkness, perhaps for the sake of saving something precious. Sometimes a gleeful tradgedy of monsters uncovered by freedom from consequence.What all these stories (and all tradgety in literature) have in common is that things inevitably decend and that the character, intentionally or not, has a hand in that. Saying 'it doesn't have to be so' completely undermines the tone and essentials of all these stories.<br /> <br /> And it's not even good for the 'heroic' story. Knowing that you're doing a certain amount of harm to the world, inevitably, and stuggling constantly to do enough good to make up for it? That has a certain element of heroism. Knowing you might be dangerous and studiously avioding those consequences? Much less so. (Not to mention being a Sidereal menthod of handling these things.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423471#post423471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is just a villain splat. It's D&amp;D's Always Chaotic Evil Drow, including the inevitable &quot;noble drow trying to redeem his evil kin&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you miss the 'deliberately created to destroy the world'? Of course they're villains. (From Cliving reation's point of view, I'm sure there's a lot that could be done to portray them as bold heoes carving out more space for the dispossessed ghosts of the Underworld). And of course they're going to come off as a defecting minority. They are literally both <i>defecting</i> and <i>a minority.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423471#post423471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of the outsider hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can appreciate that to a degree, but fulfilling this in that way you want requires ignoring the mirror between Abyssals Grand Tradgedy and the Solars Heroic Epic, and undermining all the other Abyssal stories in favor of the one you have in mind (Maybe. I still think this story works better with the Dark Fate in full force.) Perhaps the themes you're looking for will be better represented by Liminals, who appear to be outcast by design and don't have the same built-in themes to handle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","user":"SuddenThunder","date":". 03-01-2015, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T05:16:13-08:00","id":424005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423471#post423471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would prefer if the doom an Abyssal brings to the world came from them <i>slipping up</i>, with even tiny mistakes - or even simple carelessness - quickly leading to long-term or permanent damage to those around them. [Edit: Or, alternately, if they had to constantly &quot;swim against the stream&quot; - where their existence itself does bring harm in some way, but <i>not</i> irreparable harm to the fabric of creation as a whole, and where their constant effort can actually outweight the destruction they bring... for as long as they keep struggling.] I would prefer them to be <i>dangerous</i>, not <i>inevitably, invariably damaging</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly I think this sort of viewpoint is probably a common psychological waypoint on the 'Heroic Abyssal' journey. <br /> <br /> Surely if I just behave a certain way, or aviod a certain thing, or always spin the prayer wheels, or stay on holy ground ... then it'll be alright. <br /> <br /> Comign to terms with the fact that the Dark Fate can't be avioded and has to be actively opposed would be the closest thing to a universal milestone in those stories you get, I imagine. (And of course there's a fair share of those who come to realise that inevitability and collapse under it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T05:58:34-08:00","id":424036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423997#post423997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What it says is 'I can get out of it'. Sure I made this terrible deal to continue living at the expense of the world, but the consequenses of that are entirely under my control. Because I now have good intentions, I avoid all the harm I agreed to represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>They already <i>can</i> get out of it. They &quot;just&quot; have to change their colour scheme and turn golden (and get some differently-themed powers in the process). So, &quot;getting out&quot; is already an option.<br /> I'm <i>not</i> suggesting that staying an Abyssal without constantly harming the world should be easier than redemption, I'm saying it should be <i>possible</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423997#post423997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's not even good for the 'heroic' story. Knowing that you're doing a certain amount of harm to the world, inevitably, and stuggling constantly to do enough good to make up for it? That has a certain element of heroism. Knowing you might be dangerous and studiously avioding those consequences? Much less so. (Not to mention being a Sidereal menthod of handling these things.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the &quot;swimming against the stream&quot; option I included (Sure, it's an edit, but it's an edit that was already there when you quoted me and which made up half the paragraph). At the very least, in some way, the good things a suitably &quot;heroic&quot; Abyssal can do should be able to make up for the harm he does by existing - which is impossible if the harm his existence causes is permanent, while the good he does is temporary.<br /> <br /> Unless you're suggesting that for an heroic Abyssal any struggle, except the struggle for redemption, <i>has</i> to be futile. In which case I simply disagree. I think any struggle (save for &quot;Destroy X&quot; or &quot;Turn Gold&quot;, which both have fixed end points) should be constant and unending, but not <i>impossible</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423997#post423997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you miss the 'deliberately created to destroy the world'? Of course they're villains. (From Cliving reation's point of view, I'm sure there's a lot that could be done to portray them as bold heoes carving out more space for the dispossessed ghosts of the Underworld). And of course they're going to come off as a defecting minority. They are literally both <i>defecting</i> and <i>a minority.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>They're villains as much as Solars are heroes. And in case you missed it, Solars (deliberately created, depending on who you ask, to either to simply &quot;fight the enemies of the gods&quot; or to &quot;protect and rule the world&quot;) were such &quot;great&quot; heroes that TUC once gave up on the world. So yah, if they're supposed to mirror Solars, then they should mirror them <i>properly</i>. Which leads to...<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423997#post423997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can appreciate that to a degree, but fulfilling this in that way you want requires ignoring the mirror between Abyssals Grand Tradgedy and the Solars Heroic Epic,</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars can easily be some of the greatest villains in the setting - <i>without turning black.</i> If a Solar <i>doesn't</i> have to turn into an Abyssal to become a horrible blight upon creation, why does an Abyssal have to turn into a Solar to <i>stop</i> being one?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423997#post423997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and undermining all the other Abyssal stories in favor of the one you have in mind (Maybe. I still think this story works better with the Dark Fate in full force.) Perhaps the themes you're looking for will be better represented by Liminals, who appear to be outcast by design and don't have the same built-in themes to handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making Redemption optional doesn't mean making it obsolete. An heroic Abyssal would still have to struggle with his Abyssal nature (just that it would be &quot;a constant struggle&quot;, not &quot;a struggle he will inevitably lose&quot;), and Redemption would be the way out. But <i>some</i> Abyssals might decide that the powers their Abyssal nature (as opposed to a Solar one) gives them are necessary, that the continued struggle is worth it, and that they can do more good by staying on the dark side - and this shouldn't mean that they will be, in the long run, inevitably more harmful to creation then they'd be otherwise. The only difference that comes from this is that Redemption is &quot;a way out of the constant struggle and again becoming a part of the world&quot;, instead of &quot;a requirement to be a hero in the first place&quot;.<br /> (And &quot;Destroying Creation&quot; doesn't even get touched by it. If an Abyssal wants to do that, their story doesn't change in the slightest.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","user":"Dusk Shine","date":". 03-01-2015, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:19:21-08:00","id":424062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422370#post422370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Golconda in Vampire: the Masquerade was implied, at first, to allow you to become human again - or to, at least, save your soul like a human's is saved.<br /> <br /> It involved becoming an ascetic saint.<br /> <br /> Does that make a statement that humanity is inherently moral? Or just that to cast a curse to your very nature away one must be as a saint?<br /> <br /> You are drawing the wrong inference from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In comparison with the Kindred? Yes, implying that humanity was an inherently more moral state than literal Damnation was precisely the point.<br /> <br /> And I'm not drawing any inference altogether, I'm merely stating the concerns that some people have expressed in this very thread. <br /> <br /> \u200bI have no particular bone to pick with the Redemption storyline even through I'm one of those people that dislike the Unconquered Sun as a flawless paragon of virtue. I have no problem with Abyssals having to deal with him and his concept of morals to get to become Solars, I'm perfectly capable of playing him as a flawed character that demands others to conform to his idea of morality before granting them the boon of Redemption.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=422460#post422460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> First let me just say that, I am only offering you these remarks because I am trying to take your criticism to heart\u2014but it's difficult if I don't understand your meaning. Now that you have made yourself very clear, let's start again, shall we?<br /> <br /> There's nothing in a Solar's powers that makes everything they do turn out &quot;Good&quot; or moral. But the Abyssal curse guarantees everything they do will end in ash and sorrow. To an Abyssal suffering this curse, the motive/creative/holy power of Solar Exaltation represents not a guarantee of a state of moral good, but the <i>chance</i> to do moral good as he deems it, without bringing ruin and death to everyone and everything he loves as a guaranteed promise of his power. An Abyssal who wants to break the curse would rise to the lofty heights of sainthood in pursuing this goal, despite the awful price in suffering he must pay. It has everything to do with the Abyssal's idea of morality and how the Unconquered Sun recognizes a hero's virtue, and that Solars have the choice of good or evil. Redemption does not mean the Abyssal who has become a Solar will be free from temptation and unable to make mistakes or act immorally, although it is highly implied that they will stay a moral actor by virtue of what they have suffered.<br /> <br /> And yes, this all requires the ST to deem actions moral, which some may reject outright. Those kinds of Storytellers won't run Redemption stories, and that's AOK, but other Storytellers doing so won't hurt their games.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said in my response to Colapso it isn't like I particularly dislike the default setup for the Redemption storyline and, as I said in my previous post, I was more or less just pointing out that the concerns expressed to that point in the thread weren't so easily addressed just by changing the depiction of Solar NPCs... Well, I guess you just did address at least one of these concerns, so I suppose I can't complain.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:41:06-08:00","id":424075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=424036#post424036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you're suggesting that for an heroic Abyssal any struggle, except the struggle for redemption, <i>has</i> to be futile. In which case I simply disagree. I think any struggle (save for &quot;Destroy X&quot; or &quot;Turn Gold&quot;, which both have fixed end points) should be constant and unending, but not <i>impossible</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we might have slightly different grasps on our point of contention. <br /> <br /> I'm trying to say that Abyssals should always, necessarily, be doing harm to to the world, simply by existing. Even if they retire to holy ground to meditate in the hopes of containing the DarkFate. Avoiding their nature in that way is futile.The only heroic (as per Creation. There are all sorts of Dark Champion archetypes that I assume are not at issue int he discussion) thing to be doing is to actively be out there working to offset the wound that your are. Always bearing in mind that you are expicitly designed to make this difficult, and you are almost certainly going to end up blighting, cursing or horrifing people you didn't meant to somewhere along the way. <br /> <br /> So I disagree with you to the degree that you say things like 'I would prefer if the doom an Abyssal brings to the world came from them <i>slipping up' or '</i>can an Abyssal at least focus said &quot;ash and sorrow&quot; on their enemies', or ' I would prefer them to be<i>dangerous</i>, not <i>inevitably, invariably damaging</i>.'. They should absolutely be inevitibaly, invariably damaging. The Dark Fate should never be theirs to moderate, marshall or control. <br /> <br /> But it it certainly theirs to strive against, if they can bear the struggle. (And what are the Exalted good at, if not struggling against their Fate?)<br /> <br /> (Also, kinda of an aside ... but I think you discuss redemption much to simply and glibly in this thread. It's a goal that Abyssals can work towards but which no Abyssal can themselves achieve, as it requires the intervention of a being that basically can't be compelled and only haphazardly convinced. And even if sucessful, the suggestions are that it may well just invovle the Abyssal dieing and someone else becoming a new Solar. To be honest I'd be perfectly happy if redemption wasn't a thing at all, and if a player came to me wanting to do that story I'd be asking why the character was an Abyssal in the first place. It's not as though characters like Moray Darktide aren't a thing.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:02:14-08:00","id":424098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423149#post423149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, hmm.<br /> <br /> From my perspective, and this is me trying to do tea-leaf reading so it may be wrong, there are a lot of people who...<br /> <br /> 1) Would like to play an Abyssal, but...<br /> <br /> 2) Don't want them to turn into a Solar, for a variety of reasons including but not limited to rejecting the moral authority of the Unconqured Sun to declare that they're not evil and are in fact heroes,<br /> <br /> 3) Don't want to pursue the annihilation of Creation, and<br /> <br /> 4) Don't want to labor under the Abyssal Curse of everything they touch redounding to the ultimate benefit of the Neverborn.<br /> <br /> This has always kind of baffled me. The whole point of playing an Abyssal, it has always seemed to me, is that you agreed to the agenda of Oblivion, for whatever reason, and now you have to decide between either serving that agenda with your whole heart, or rejecting it and starting the long slow climb towards redemption and returning the Black Exaltation you bear to its true state, free of the taint of the Neverborn. There's always been a potential third path, where you decide to usurp the Deathlords and then just not pursue Oblivion, but the Underworld by its very nature serves Oblivion, so... yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my perspective, and this may sound shallow, the point is to be a goth superhuman in Exalted's genre, who can invoke the power of death in support of any skill or disciple.<br /> <br /> The stuff about dooming the world and causing suffering to random innocent bystanders is not so interesting - &quot;Woe, woe, must the taint of my power corrupt all that is good!&quot;. <br /> <br /> The real appeal of Abyssals to me do not seem really about that at its core, in terms of their primary draw, any more than being the appeal of being a fire aspect is that you doom the world to eventually be consumed by a fiery wasteland, or being a water aspect is about bringing the great flood or even how being a Fair Folk necessarily means being bound to inevitably dissolve Creation in the Wyld, rather than being a clever, powerful prince of chaos.<br /> <br /> Still, given redemption as a theme, for Abyssals, I do think redemption would be more satisfying if there was something in the Abyssals that specifically tied them to the service of the Deathlords and Neverborn - I don't like this setup where the Abyssal can divorce himself from the service of the Deathlords and then resonance occurs and random powers reach out into the world. Feels unsatisfying. I think it's that feel where resonance feels randomly &quot;rubber banded&quot; on to the character of the Abyssals, a glue on that it is easy to imagine an Abyssal without, that damages the idea of redemption. It feels like an arbitrary thing put in the world to force heroism to focus on Solars, rather than a natural consequence of the Abyssal power.<br /> <br /> It just has that feel of arbitrary magic rather than a logical connection - there's nothing in the character's personality or his social relationships which is acting. You can contrast to the Star Wars &quot;Dark Side of the Force&quot; that is trying to be emulated, where the dark power the person is wielding reaches out through the to corrupt their actions or force them into social relationships with people bent on destruction. Even being haunted by a specific spirit or deathbrining specific spirits connected to the Abyssal's actions might be better than the way resonance works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:22:02-08:00","id":424132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423149#post423149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the Underworld by its very nature serves Oblivion, so... yeah.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it shouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:39:30-08:00","id":424147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423612#post423612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the idea that an individual retains a recognizable value of self-hood from incarnation to incarnation questionable at best.<br /> <br /> Plenty of religions and philosophies in Creation and the real world believe otherwise, but the setting doesn't specifically give you an answer one way or another.<br /> <br /> Coupling this with the fact that more than a few of the terrible acts in Creation have been justified with &quot;we'll give them a better deal in the next life&quot; seems to me to show that reincarnation isn't the natural and numinous principle it's chalked up to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>The purpose of reincarnation has <i><b>nothing</b></i> to do with preserving the conscious mind and personality that Westerners believe is the center of selfhood. But I'm not going to derail the thread by trying to argue.<br /> <br /> As for your final paragraph ... WTF strawman? I don't even know what you're saying but I don't advocate mass murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-01-2015, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:48:38-08:00","id":424155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=424075#post424075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we might have slightly different grasps on our point of contention.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to say that Abyssals should always, necessarily, be doing harm to to the world, simply by existing. Even if they retire to holy ground to meditate in the hopes of containing the DarkFate. Avoiding their nature in that way is futile.The only heroic (as per Creation. There are all sorts of Dark Champion archetypes that I assume are not at issue int he discussion) thing to be doing is to actively be out there working to offset the wound that your are. Always bearing in mind that you are expicitly designed to make this difficult, and you are almost certainly going to end up blighting, cursing or horrifing people you didn't meant to somewhere along the way.<br /> <br /> So I disagree with you to the degree that you say things like 'I would prefer if the doom an Abyssal brings to the world came from them <i>slipping up' or '</i>can an Abyssal at least focus said &quot;ash and sorrow&quot; on their enemies', or ' I would prefer them to be<i>dangerous</i>, not <i>inevitably, invariably damaging</i>.'. They should absolutely be inevitibaly, invariably damaging. The Dark Fate should never be theirs to moderate, marshall or control.<br /> <br /> But it it certainly theirs to strive against, if they can bear the struggle. (And what are the Exalted good at, if not struggling against their Fate?)</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, the &quot; only when slipping up&quot;/&quot;focusing on their enemies&quot; parts... weren't my best ideas. I do prefer the &quot;needs constant struggle to offset the damage they do&quot;-version.<br /> What I really dislike is the idea that they can <i>never</i> offset the damage they do, because that literally says &quot;turn gold or be a villain&quot;. And if the damage is permanent while the good they do is temporary, then they never can - so in a way, heroic Abyssals need to either be able to create &quot;lasting goodness&quot;, which is out of theme for Exalted (everything good fades with time), or the damage they do needs to be... well, not stuff that can be undone, because &quot;undoing stuff&quot; is also out of theme for Exalted, but stuff that can be &quot;healed&quot; or &quot;replaced&quot; (like shadowlands which can be turned normal again ( very slowly by mortal means, more quickly by sorcery), or kingdoms that can be rebuild - though either or both might be impossible to the Abyssal himself. Hurray for a reason for cross-splat alliances!).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=424075#post424075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, kinda of an aside ... but I think you discuss redemption much to simply and glibly in this thread. It's a goal that Abyssals can work towards but which no Abyssal can themselves achieve, as it requires the intervention of a being that basically can't be compelled and only haphazardly convinced. And even if sucessful, the suggestions are that it may well just invovle the Abyssal dieing and someone else becoming a new Solar. To be honest I'd be perfectly happy if redemption wasn't a thing at all, and if a player came to me wanting to do that story I'd be asking why the character was an Abyssal in the first place. It's not as though characters like Moray Darktide aren't a thing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Redemption is presented as a possibility, even if it's only possible by constantly struggleing until it is achived, maybe only in death. I'd like &quot;heroic Abyssal&quot; to be equally possible - even though it might just be even harder, because a redeemed Abyssals struggle ends (or at least gets reduced to &quot;regular&quot; heroic struggle) no matter whether turn golden or die, while the struggle of an heroic Abyssal <i>without</i> redemption <i>definitely</i> continues until death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:36:23-08:00","id":424294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=424147#post424147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The purpose of reincarnation has <i><b>nothing</b></i> to do with preserving the conscious mind and personality that Westerners believe is the center of selfhood. But I'm not going to derail the thread by trying to argue.<br /> <br /> As for your final paragraph ... WTF strawman? I don't even know what you're saying but I don't advocate mass murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really a side argument, if your character doesn't believe that his or her reincarnation is qualifiably themselves, then the soul isn't much of anything, and its destruction doesn't mean much.<br /> <br /> I realize most of the cultures in Creation adhere to reincarnation, but I don't think that's anymore of an absolute value in the setting than looking at the Unconquered Sun as an unquestionable and numinous moral authority. That isn't to say that either is a right or wrong, just that it's a view.<br /> <br /> Exalted is big enough to have a bunch religious views, and neither of them are objectively correct or incorrect.<br /> <br /> As for the last paragraph, I apologize for my wording, I didn't intend to accuse you of anything or equate your or anyone else's beliefs to that of those sociopaths. My point was Exalted approaches religion in a really cynical way, and raises its eyebrows at the idea of any ontological belief. I would lump the idea of identity post-reincarnation in that particular category, just like I'd lump a lot of other religious ideas. My point was to show that where there's religion in Exalted, you can generally follow the money (prayer, obedience, whatever) back to someone in power getting their ends.<br /> <br /> There's room for reincarnation to be right, but I think there's also room for it to be wrong, or for it to be something ineffable and in-between and impossible to qualify in an absolute sense.<br /> <br /> Is this less objectionable? I've been enjoying the discussion so far and it's not my intention to offend you or anyone else =\\","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":". 03-01-2015, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:06:23-08:00","id":424309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=423997#post423997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the consequenses of that are entirely under my control. Because I now have good intentions, I avoid all the harm I agreed to represent.<br /> <br /> Saying 'it doesn't have to be so' completely undermines the tone and essentials of all these stories.<br /> <br /> And it's not even good for the 'heroic' story. Knowing that you're doing a certain amount of harm to the world, inevitably, and stuggling constantly to do enough good to make up for it? That has a certain element of heroism. Knowing you might be dangerous and studiously avioding those consequences? Much less so. (Not to mention being a Sidereal menthod of handling these things.)<br /> <br /> Did you miss the 'deliberately created to destroy the world'? Of course they're villains. (From Cliving reation's point of view, I'm sure there's a lot that could be done to portray them as bold heoes carving out more space for the dispossessed ghosts of the Underworld). And of course they're going to come off as a defecting minority. They are literally both <i>defecting</i> and <i>a minority.</i><br /> <br /> I can appreciate that to a degree, but fulfilling this in that way you want requires ignoring the mirror between Abyssals Grand Tradgedy and the Solars Heroic Epic, and undermining all the other Abyssal stories in favor of the one you have in mind (Maybe. I still think this story works better with the Dark Fate in full force.) Perhaps the themes you're looking for will be better represented by Liminals, who appear to be outcast by design and don't have the same built-in themes to handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Exalted is a game about consequences, but I also believe that Exalted is a game that speaks to the consequences of actions rather than thought, bargain or fate.<br /> <br /> My ideal Exalted scorns irrefutable truths. A character can believe that just the existence of any given Abyssal inevitably dooms the world, and maybe they're right, but the presence of a possible doubt seems like a vital thing to me, and a dubious thing to remove.<br /> <br /> Further, I don't want it to seem like I'm saying there should be no consequences for an Abyssal that spurns redemption. <b>They are</b> no longer human. It's likely that many of the things that once held joy for them don't any longer, the small and precious things that mortals take for granted are lost on them in a way that other Exalted never suffer.<br /> <br /> <b>There should always be a specter of anguish haunting the Abyssal like a second shadow, gnawing at their person no matter how ancient or enlightened</b> (whatever that means) <b>they become.</b><br /> <br /> However, I think expressing this anguish as &quot;my existence, one way or another, inevitably dooms all Creation to ashes&quot; is a shallow representation. It seems played out, disconnected from the sorts of problems that people actually face. It feels clumsy and ham-handed to me. *shrug* I suppose that's just a matter of taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:06:35-08:00","id":424310,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry I misinterpreted your last paragraph; I didn't understand it.<br /> <br /> I agree that religion in Exalted is always or almost always cynical. Part of the argument that the setting is &quot;grimdark&quot; or even &quot;shitdark&quot; is that the gods are all universally depicted as such corrupt assholes that there's nothing left in Yu Shan or Creation worth saving. I think that's not entirely true, but I do agree that there's nothing in inherently morally right or even natural about an order created by the Primordials and/or enforced by selfish, corrupt gods. Human reincarnation seems like a raw deal in a world where keeping more continuity of personality or memory, or just contact with your loved ones, could have been a design option for humanity. (But then again, seeing how well <i><b>that</b></i> worked out for the Dragon Kings, maybe humanity is better off with memory-erasing Lethe!)<br /> <br /> Different cultures in the real world, and presumably in Creation, emphasize different things as the core of the concept of self. A soul that reincarnates without memory isn't necessarily a new person, it's all a question of what people believe. Since humans have two souls, and Celestial Exalted have a third soul that reincarnates separately from their other souls but does carry some of their memories and identity into the future, and fuse with somebody else's mortal souls, the whole question of human selfhood gets even more complicated. It's no longer just a question of which part is the core of the self, it's also a question of whether self is indivisible, or divisible and even re-combinable. Desus died, and I don't know where his mortal souls went, but let's assume his hun (higher soul) became the Silver Prince and his po (lower soul) is either still stuck to his corpse somewhere, or soulforged. His exaltation fused with a totally separate human soul (Swan). Which of these three, if any, is the &quot;same&quot; self as Desus? Is the Solar named Swan the same self as the mortal guy who used to be Swan, or a separate new person? The Deathlords each fused with a piece of a Neverborn (or something, I'm not clear on this). Does that make them a new, separate self from the dead dude who was merely a ghost? If Desus' hun has instead reincarnated as a new mortal with new memories and identity and a new po, is he Desus or a new self? If he gets a different exaltation fused into his po, is he yet another new self, or a continuation of that exaltation's past life's self, or a continuation of his mortal self? If he exalts Infernal and also has a demon fused into his soul as a voice in his head, is he a new self that combined the human and demon selves, and if so which human self/selves? If somebody digs up Desus' tomb and accidentally turns his corpse into a Liminal who has some of Desus' memories, who is <i><b>that</b></i> now? Is the entire concept of a defined &quot;self&quot; with boundaries merely an illusion?<br /> <br /> I don't know if the majority belief in Creation even is to prefer reincarnation -- how numerous are ancestor cults outside the Immaculate sphere of influence? I guess probably fewer people than Immaculate believers. Some people may prefer to have an afterlife in the Underworld, some may prefer to reincarnate, and some may believe and want something else that doesn't necessarily even exist. Sol Invictus turns some dead people into spirits in the Daystar.<br /> <br /> Regardless, destroying a soul deprives them of any of those options. I think that's more horrific and probably more wrong then most other options, unless their afterlife was going to be one of such terrible suffering that destroying them is mercy by comparison. Not that Exalted has anyone going around torturously soulforging dead people into globs of pure metallic agony for eternity... <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">I am bad at marking sarcasm. That sentence was sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> But some interpretations of Buddhism and/or Adorjan's philosophy suggest that any existence as a person is suffering and ending any existence is mercy. So if the Immaculate Philosophy is Cynical Evil Hinduism, the Neverborn and Adorjan are pushing Cynical Evil Buddhism. (Adorjan makes questions about the definition of self even more confusing with the Shintai that enables <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/414190-1-infernal-an-entire-martial-arts-ninja-clan-of-super-mortals-covering-creation\">these shenanigans</a>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-01-2015, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T02:48:00-08:00","id":424980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=424309#post424309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>There should always be a specter of anguish haunting the Abyssal like a second shadow, gnawing at their person no matter how ancient or enlightened</b> (whatever that means) <b>they become.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, and I think this represents a basic misattrtibution of intent. The point of the Dark Fate isn't to punish the Abyssal, it's to punish the world. <br /> <br /> You can be Hamlet, and contemlate the fundamental decay of your house, asking whether suicide is the best thing that you can possibly do, but you can also be Arthas, massacring the peasantry, 'suceeding you', and going on to lay waste to the kingdom, largely comfortable in the fact that everything you've done was right. You can be on either side of the 'Vampire Hunter D: Bloodlines' story, either a child of profane powers making their way through the world yet inevitably leaving a trail of corpses, or the predatory monster willing to sacrifice more of less whatever in order to preserve one beautiful thing. <br /> <br /> Abyssal stories are always tradgeties but the tradgety doesn't have to fall on the Abyssals shoulders. They don't have to be horribly tortured and remorseful about the things that happen around them, at their hands or otherwise. Most of them, in fact, probably aren't. Abyssals are all people willing to exchange their own continued existence for the diminishement of Creation, after all. They have every reason not to be upset about that. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T06:49:50-08:00","id":425118,"title":"","content":"T-R-A-G-E-D-Y. Tragedy, from the Greek &quot;trag\u014didia.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:White\">&quot;Getimians,&quot; being a nonstandard word, I can understand being misspelled. &quot;Tragedy,&quot; though, is something you can at least look up.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T07:26:52-08:00","id":425160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=424980#post424980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree, and I think this represents a basic misattrtibution of intent. The point of the Dark Fate isn't to punish the Abyssal, it's to punish the world. <br /> <br /> You can be Hamlet, and contemlate the fundamental decay of your house, asking whether suicide is the best thing that you can possibly do, but you can also be Arthas, massacring the peasantry, 'suceeding you', and going on to lay waste to the kingdom, largely comfortable in the fact that everything you've done was right. You can be on either side of the 'Vampire Hunter D: Bloodlines' story, either a child of profane powers making their way through the world yet inevitably leaving a trail of corpses, or the predatory monster willing to sacrifice more of less whatever in order to preserve one beautiful thing. <br /> <br /> Abyssal stories are always tradgeties but the tradgety doesn't have to fall on the Abyssals shoulders. They don't have to be horribly tortured and remorseful about the things that happen around them, at their hands or otherwise. Most of them, in fact, probably aren't. Abyssals are all people willing to exchange their own continued existence for the diminishement of Creation, after all. They have every reason not to be upset about that. </div> </div> </div> </div>You mistake the fundamental principle of my discontent, my argument is that inevitability of consequences, especially as expressed in the binary of &quot;enjoy making everything thing worse or feel deservedly like a shit because your very existence is inevitably poisonous to Creation.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about Hamlet, he's a schmuck who shirked his duty in the name of temperance. More to the point, Hamlet isn't a story that presents much opportunity for player agency, given the whole damn thing is about our inability to escape the ineffable and unescapable qualities of justice and death. <br /> <br /> Neither Arthas nor Hamlet is an interesting character arc to me. Neither story interacts with the story I'd like to tell with this potential Abyssal character arc in my head.<br /> <br /> Look, we're not going to change one another's minds on this. I think a splat which makes a statement about the inevitable destiny and summation of its characters is face-palm level stupidity, you obviously disagree. This isn't a failure to understand the setting on either of our parts, just different, unfortunately exclusive, tastes concerning what Abyssal stories could or couldn't be.<br /> <br /> To beat the horse into paste, this is not a misunderstanding. It's a statement of opinion concerning what I feel to be a childish and uninteresting shoe-horn. Disagree if you want, but I'm not &quot;misattributing&quot; anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":". 03-02-2015, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T07:34:05-08:00","id":425167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425160#post425160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the binary of &quot;enjoy making everything thing worse or feel deservedly like a shit because your very existence is inevitably poisonous to Creation.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that like that wasn't the entire point. <br /> <br /> I mean, what did you think the Neverborn would make them do? Shit puppies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T07:43:44-08:00","id":425169,"title":"","content":"This is also potentially why the Abyssals are getting Deathlord-themed charms in 3e, instead of Oblivion-themed charms - being the agent of a Deathlord isn't <i>automatically</i> a blight on creation, though it still can be (and probably is so in most cases).<br /> <br /> I see the Agent of Oblivion thing in the same light as Burn Life (but on a grander scale). It's there if you want to focus on the life-ending aspect of it, otherwise it's on a waaay too long a scale to matter to every Abyssal, even ones that want to do good after realizing they took a bad deal.<br /> <br /> If they stay in the underworld to be the guardians of ghosts, they're not hurting anyone. If they're out in creation, the necrosis they cause isn't obvious unless they specifically try to go all-out existence-slaying nether-monsters.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of other ways for a character to rationalize it away too (which may or may not be correct): the wyld may be replenishishing Creation in some way, the poles might have reality-restorative properties, they might even believe that the &quot;blight&quot; of their powers is too insignificant to compare to the scope of all Creation (except when they explode in shadowland-creating destruction) and so doesn't warrant much thought, etc.<br /> <br /> So it's not like anyone is forced to focus on it. But it's there for those that want to, and it fits with the story of the game and the modus operandi of the never-dead titanic souls of the creators of the cosmos who want nothing less than to end all existence so their infinite torment can end with it.<br /> <br /> Whether or not the mechanics were well handled is a different story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 03-02-2015, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:05:27-08:00","id":425209,"title":"","content":"I agree that it would make more options for Abyssal games. I do wonder (from a purely in-universe perspective) how it would be the modus operandi of the Neverborn to make it possible (or less difficult) for Abyssals to avoid blighting all Creation by their very existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:10:57-08:00","id":425228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425209#post425209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder (from a purely in-universe perspective) how it would be the modus operandi of the Neverborn to make it possible (or less difficult) for Abyssals to avoid blighting all Creation by their very existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe their un-death made them unable to interact with Exaltations the way Yozis can, so they had the Deathlords do it for them, and the Deathlords took advantage of the situation to inject their own ideals and plans which in turn diluted the Neverborn's original purpose? Or something. Idunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 03-02-2015, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:36:08-08:00","id":425245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425209#post425209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> do wonder (from a purely in-universe perspective) how it would be the modus operandi of the Neverborn to make it possible (or less difficult) for Abyssals to avoid blighting all Creation by their very existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually the simplest part: It isn't their modus operandi. The Neverborn made &quot;not killing everything ever&quot; as hard as they possibly could. But they couldn't make it completely impossible, because [ Exalts surpass those that make them | the Imperishable Light of the UCS still burns even in the corrupted Exaltations | no-one ever got exactly what they wanted out of their Exalts | whatever else floats your boat ].<br /> <br /> That, or, in some dark corner of their sundered and thorn appart multitude of souls they actually don't want to kill creation, they just want relief and rest, but they have... issues... expressing themselves. The Abyssals were still made to free them, but not by throwing Creation into Oblivion, but by some more obscure method. Plot hook! (Both options might be true, even. Or the &quot;Abyssals can put the Neverborn to rest without destroying creation&quot;-option is true, but it's something the Neverborn never expected.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","user":"Dusk Shine","date":". 03-02-2015, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:24:58-08:00","id":425296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425245#post425245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, or, in some dark corner of their sundered and thorn appart multitude of souls they actually don't want to kill creation, they just want relief and rest, but they have... issues... expressing themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding of the Neverborn has always been that, indeed, relief and rest are their priority goals. It's just that as far as I know there has never been an alternative expressed (canonically) for this other than killing Creation, which would allow them to finally fall into Oblivion and achieve that relief. They would certainly welcome any kind of alternative that is a shorter path to relief than killing all of Creation; indeed, I have always imagined that if you showed up in their tombs with a whiteboard outlining how they could get what they wanted easier than their current plans, they would shower you with power and glory such as they have access to, because you've just done them a great service.<br /> <br /> They don't just want to kill everything because they want to kill everything, it's just the shortest path from A to B for them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:31:48-08:00","id":425323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425296#post425296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding of the Neverborn has always been that, indeed, relief and rest are their priority goals. It's just that as far as I know there has never been an alternative expressed (canonically) for this other than killing Creation, which would allow them to finally fall into Oblivion and achieve that relief. They would certainly welcome any kind of alternative that is a shorter path to relief than killing all of Creation; indeed, I have always imagined that if you showed up in their tombs with a whiteboard outlining how they could get what they wanted easier than their current plans, they would shower you with power and glory such as they have access to, because you've just done them a great service.<br /> <br /> They don't just want to kill everything because they want to kill everything, it's just the shortest path from A to B for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the thing is also, that's just either their in-setting theory, or an OOC point about their belief. It's not provably true, obviously - though it stands to reason that Creation is a giant Fetter that prevents them from passing on, it's also true that the extinction of all things might do jack shit to alleviate their suffering. It wasn't my impression that even canon said &quot;yeah do this and they'll be able to pass on&quot; - IIRC that was still only presented as a possibility, just one that the Neverborn believe to be true and thus work toward that end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:38:16-08:00","id":425327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425323#post425323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the thing is also, that's just either their in-setting theory, or an OOC point about their belief. It's not provably true, obviously - though it stands to reason that Creation is a giant Fetter that prevents them from passing on, it's also true that the extinction of all things might do jack shit to alleviate their suffering. It wasn't my impression that even canon said &quot;yeah do this and they'll be able to pass on&quot; - IIRC that was still only presented as a possibility, just one that the Neverborn believe to be true and thus work toward that end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected on the terminology, Zel, although I'm not sure that Creation meets the requirements for a Fetter; I don't think the Neverborn are Fettered per se, it's just that their souls are too grand to either enter Lethe and be reborn or to fall into Oblivion and be destroyed. This isn't quite the same as being Fettered, I don't think.<br /> <br /> Good point about the other stuff, though. I should have hedged more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:43:34-08:00","id":425329,"title":"","content":"Or they want to kill creation so that they enter the wild and maybe come back to life. As much as dead things can want and plan anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:51:11-08:00","id":425359,"title":"","content":"I thought it was also spite and hate and revenge, at least as a side motivation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:52:25-08:00","id":425362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425327#post425327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stand corrected on the terminology, Zel, although I'm not sure that Creation meets the requirements for a Fetter; I don't think the Neverborn are Fettered per se, it's just that their souls are too grand to either enter Lethe and be reborn or to fall into Oblivion and be destroyed. This isn't quite the same as being Fettered, I don't think.<br /> <br /> Good point about the other stuff, though. I should have hedged more.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I could have sworn the actual terminology of &quot;Fetter&quot; was used with regard to the relationship of the Neverborn to Creation, at least hypothetically/in an OOC context.<br /> <br /> At any rate, it being a Fetter to me is the only thing that really makes sense about why they can't pass on. It's not like destroying Creation is going to &quot;widen&quot; Lethe or the Mouth of Oblivion such that they can &quot;fit&quot; through either, as far as I can tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:52:56-08:00","id":425363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425167#post425167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say that like that wasn't the entire point. <br /> <br /> I mean, what did you think the Neverborn would make them do? Shit puppies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh yes, because each of the Chosen is tied inextricably to the motive behind their creation.<br /> <br /> No . . Wait, that isn't actually the case. See previous posts concerning my thoughts on the possibility of the Abyssals uniqe interaction with the Neverborn and the possible ways that can be turned into a redemption story arc that has nothing to do with the Unconquered Sun and everything to do with aleviating suffering and reconciling the history of violence that diminishes Creation.<br /> <br /> I think it's interesting when what a character chooses to do has a greater impact on who or what they are.<br /> <br /> I understand what your saying, I'm just wholly uninterested in that kind of story. I find it justifies a particular sort of violence and diminishes the narrative of the Neverborn as sort of sympathetic. <br /> <br /> This is not to say that this is all or even a majority of 'what they are' in the setting, but I feel like this is an interesting possible story. Anyway, I find it a hell of a lot more intersting than' the solution to the Neverborn problem is to kill them harder'<br /> <br /> This sounds to me like one of the very things Exalted goes to such lengths to examine, that violence is a quick and dirty solution that diminishes both the target and perpetrator.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying anyone in Creation (especially not an abyssal) should be a pacifist, or that &quot;not-murder&quot; should be espoused as the best solution to any problem.<br /> <br /> I am saying that Soul Breaker Orbing the landscape until nothing is left shouldn't feel like the only reasonable solution. I feel your view limits the Underworld to just that toxic place which should be wiped from existence at the earliest opportunity. <br /> <br /> Sidebar, screw the Void. What's less interesting (to me) than immutable horixon size monsters screaming their undying fury forever? A nearly infinitely powered reality eating black hole which anyone capable of rubbing two brain cells together understands as a thing which should be avoided/sealed away/destroyed (if such a thing is possible).<br /> <br /> And I don't mind particular ghosts or deathlords worshipping the Void, there are extremists in any group. I'm just against the idea that any group of individuals are tied to some ineffable and inescapable value fact. Slave to Destiny or unwilling pawn is a state that's subjected onto individuals in the setting, as a result of one individual trying to get their ends. The idea that Abyssals alone are cursed, as a result of what they deserve, seems to undercut Exalteds consequentialist value rather than reinforce it.<br /> <br /> As a setting, Exalted upends the idea that anyone gets what they deserve, every other facet of the setting works in this way.<br /> <br /> This puts Abyssals in this unique category of objectively evil no matter their actions unless they change their particular supernatural clan.<br /> <br /> The Abyssals particular supernatural clan, however, also includes ghosts, the ancestor cult, all the stories and motifs that make up Underworld myths. So if I want to play in that wheelhouse, I'd like to be able to without the albatross of &quot;objectivily evil blight upon all existence&quot; hanging around my characters neck.<br /> <br /> The Neverborn created the Abyssals specifically to destroy all Creation? So what? Last time I checked there were no absolute detetminors in the setting. Further, given that the Underworld is made up of a reflection of Creation and the Tomb-Bodies of the Neverborn, yet the Underworld has certain aspects which are not inherently inimical to sentient exsistence, I'd posit that the Neverborn are more than the undying rage bellowing out of their cyclopean crypt-mouths. <br /> <br /> That's not really ancillary to my point. My point is no charactet or force in the setting gets to predetetmine the events of the future. Direct actions direct fate, not some ontological statement about whether an Indivividual is going to inevitably doom Creation.<br /> <br /> And as other posters have pointed out, if one's existence certifiably word-of-author drags Creation to inevitable and total destruction, that's about as close to &quot;evil&quot; as one gets. Such an existence means that the best thing for everyone is to kill them en masse, and if that doesn't work to kill them harder until they don't come back.<br /> <br /> Now, the Deathlords are this way, but since there are only 13 of them, they're not player splats, and the Neverborn had a direct connection to them I'm not opposed to it.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> But given your reply, I get the feeling you're a cut the Gordian Knot sort of guy, here's a tldr response for you. The Neverborn intended their Abyssals to act a certain way? So? Crap in one hand and wish on the other, see which fills up faster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":".  so much editing! 03-02-2015, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:05:03-08:00","id":425369,"title":"","content":"I figured the Neverborn reached their decision (as much as they are capable of making a decision in their state) as the best way (revenge) while getting what they really want (rest, true death, etc).<br /> <br /> I like to think the Neverborn, or an echo of the Primordial they were, also exsist as The Dual Monarchy, the Calendar of Setesh, the collective unconscious of every ghost in exsistence.<br /> <br /> I mean the &quot;biggest&quot; and most active err, part is certainly the mad rage of Whispers and incalculable malice and pain at their inconceivable state. But, I figure why not make 'em more interesting, add some depth to their width.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":". 03-02-2015, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:06:29-08:00","id":425373,"title":"","content":"You know what?<br /> <br /> I think I'm finally completely sold on the idea that Abyssals should just <b><i>never</i></b> have been written to inevitably destroy Creation even against their wills. It's as crappy as rewriting Infernals to inevitably cause the Reclamation to suceed just by existing even when they try to rebel. I'll take Dusk Shine's explanations about why this could be possible.<br /> <br /> I love the idea that Abyssals could actually discover ways to put the Neverborn to rest without destroying Creation. A high-Compassion, high-Whispers Abyssal who wants to protect the ancestor cults' interests (thus not destroy Creation) but feels absolutely driven to relieve the Neverborn's suffering could totally go for that. And it would be very interesting/profound if the narrative arc of an Abyssal was the one that found a solution to Creation's problems other than &quot;kill thine enemy some more.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mind, I still think that it should be <b><i>hard</i></b> for Abyssals to avoid being agents of destruction and blight and death, and to escape the logic of the organizations that train and equip them that killing stuff is the answer to whatever problems the Deathlords and/or Neverborn face tonight. But it just shouldn't be impossible.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: If Exalted were a novel or Abyssals had never been intended as PCs, I would still find the inevitability more plausible given the Neverborn's goals, but it's a crappy thing for a PC splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-02-2015, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:20:09-08:00","id":425385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425329#post425329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or they want to kill creation so that they enter the wild and maybe come back to life. As much as dead things can want and plan anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it was mentioned somewhere as a possible explanation for FAFL iniciating the Fair Folk invasion (which, apparently, is the reason the Great Contagion became curable, thus one Apocalypse (The Great Contagion) became neutralised by another, simpler one (Balor's Crusade) which was solvable - and solved - by brute force):<br /> He always claimed the Neverborn told him to do that. Turns out, they might have: A possible reason given was that they wanted creation to be swallowed by the Wyld (not destroyed) so in the realm of infinite possibility, they may break Exalted's big golden &quot;No Backsies&quot;-rule.<br /> <br /> That being said, Yes to both &quot;The Neverborn just want to stop being in eternal pain (Creation is just collateral)&quot; and &quot;The Neverborn broke Reincarnation&quot;.<br /> It's been stated that before them, there was no Underworld - their death broke the circle of reincarnation. Whatever mystical mechanisms (Lethe) they put in place to process the dead couldn't handle them because their own (proper, non-fetich) death was inconcievable to them (I like to say &quot;the drain broke because something to big got stuffed in, now it leaks&quot;).<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, it's also been stated that the &quot;orders&quot; the Neverborn give are... often cryptic. It's generaly accepted that they really <i>do</i> seek Creation's destruction (and it has been compared to a Fetter), but a never canonically mentioned alternate character interpretation (read: A random idea I just had) might just be that when they order &quot;complete destruction&quot;, it never refers to Creation. They actually <i>don't</i> want to destroy Creation, they really just created the Deathlords so someone would find a way to end them, but the Deathlords only understood &quot;Death&quot; and &quot;End&quot;, and went &quot;Well, sure, let's End Creation by killing everything!&quot;. So, the Neverborn are actually pretty pissed of because the Deathlords are such assholes about the whole thing and do stuff the Neverborn never actually wanted them to do.<br /> I would hate for this to be the official canon, but leaving it a possibility (by never going into to much detail) seems fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","user":"Dusk Shine","date":". 03-02-2015, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:40:54-08:00","id":425415,"title":"","content":"Given that the Neverborn are slain primordials, I think it's reasonable for them to hold contradictory thoughts at the same time. Rather than thinking of them as independent actors capable of holding coherent thoughts.<br /> <br /> Some of a given NB's pieces just want to burn it all down because of the pain, some want revenge, some don't think exsistence is worth anything since it lost x or y... Culpability or responsibility, or even things like rational thought are while not necessarily absent, but definitely hyper-alien.<br /> <br /> Like a pseudo-sentient necro-earthquake with the a staggering case of PTSD, what they want or are even capable of wanting is . . Complicated<br /> <br /> My views are partially inspired by The Other in Tad Williams Otherland novels. Not a one-for-one equivalence, but it brings interesting ideas to the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:43:37-08:00","id":425417,"title":"","content":"Hell, one of them had doubts about his own existence back when he was alive anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:50:12-08:00","id":425420,"title":"","content":"(Also: Damn it. Why isn't there a &quot;pause&quot;-button for the internet. I type <i>one</i> response, and there's an entirely new page already!)<br /> (And also:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425373#post425373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll take Dark Shine's explanations [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, but it's <i>Dusk</i> Shine =P Gender-swapped version of Twilight Sparkle. I was a lot more into MLP when I made this account then I am now.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:16:08-08:00","id":425437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425420#post425420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was a lot more into MLP when I made this account then I am now</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to be bashful, you'd be surprised how many <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-here-be-ponies\">fans of the show</a> these forums contain.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:30:39-08:00","id":425446,"title":"","content":"Oops, sorry Dusk Shine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:12:21-08:00","id":425530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425415#post425415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the Neverborn are slain primordials, I think it's reasonable for them to hold contradictory thoughts at the same time. Rather than thinking of them as independent actors capable of holding coherent thoughts.<br /> <br /> Some of a given NB's pieces just want to burn it all down because of the pain, some want revenge, some don't think exsistence is worth anything since it lost x or y... Culpability or responsibility, or even things like rational thought are while not necessarily absent, but definitely hyper-alien.<br /> <br /> Like a pseudo-sentient necro-earthquake with the a staggering case of PTSD, what they want or are even capable of wanting is . . Complicated<br /> <br /> My views are partially inspired by The Other in Tad Williams Otherland novels. Not a one-for-one equivalence, but it brings interesting ideas to the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also had the idea once that Neverborn weren't actually &quot;dead&quot;, per se (which, in fact, also explains the term <i>Un</i>dead), but merely &quot;crippled&quot; Primordials.<br /> In this concept for Primordials, said Primordials are independant of their Jouten-bodies. Jouten were more like libs, used to interact with the world, but the Primordial itself was outside of existence. Also, each Primordial had a limit to how many Jouten could manifest at once. Solars &quot;killing&quot; Primordials merely destroyed their Jouten permanently, reducing the number of Jouten a Primordial could manifest.<br /> The Neverborn were Primordials who lost all their Jouten, which left them unable to interact with the world. This &quot;untethered&quot; them from the world, but the &quot;metaphysical weight&quot; of their titan-souls attracts lesser (read: mortal) souls, creating the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425417#post425417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, one of them had doubts about his own existence back when he was alive anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not doubts about his existence, doubts about his identity. He didn't ask &quot;Am I?&quot;, he asked &quot;<i>Who</i> am I?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425437#post425437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No need to be bashful</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm not bashful. I like a lot of &quot;weird&quot; stuff, be it Disney's Frozen or this Bronze Age power fantasy RPG called Exalted. It's just that by now, I've mostly returned to using &quot;Yuuto Amakawa&quot; (based on one of my favourite manga) as a nick in most places - I just don't want to make a new account here, and don't think I","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T15:08:46-08:00","id":425716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/409432-solar-redemption-in-3e?p=425437#post425437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No need to be bashful, you'd be surprised how many <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3197-h